1
00:02:17,446 --> 00:02:19,485
Let me go!

2
00:02:19,486 --> 00:02:20,885
Alaeddin Bey!

3
00:02:30,286 --> 00:02:33,085
Mother..

4
00:02:42,966 --> 00:02:44,005
No...

5
00:03:00,966 --> 00:03:03,885
Mother..

6
00:03:12,646 --> 00:03:13,885
Mother!

7
00:03:13,886 --> 00:03:16,925
Mother, don't do this! Mother!

8
00:03:16,926 --> 00:03:18,965
Mother! Don't do this to me, mother!

9
00:03:18,966 --> 00:03:22,725
Don't leave your children
motherless and us helpless, mother!

10
00:03:22,726 --> 00:03:26,445
Mother!

11
00:03:28,326 --> 00:03:31,125
Mother! What happened to your hands, mother?

12
00:03:31,486 --> 00:03:35,525
What happened to you? What
did they do to you? Mother...

13
00:03:36,366 --> 00:03:39,365
My Allah, how cruel is this...

14
00:03:39,366 --> 00:03:42,405
How..

15
00:03:42,446 --> 00:03:46,765
Mother! What happened to your
eyes that used to be bright, mother?

16
00:03:46,766 --> 00:03:47,925
What happened mother?

17
00:03:47,926 --> 00:03:50,445
What did they do to you, mother?

18
00:03:52,806 --> 00:03:56,525
How? How?

19
00:03:56,526 --> 00:03:59,725
How did they make the
light in your eyes disappear?

20
00:03:59,726 --> 00:04:03,245
How? How did they do it?
-Who did this?

21
00:04:04,526 --> 00:04:08,325
Who did this?!

22
00:04:11,806 --> 00:04:13,365
Begum Hatun, my Bey.

23
00:04:19,245 --> 00:04:20,524
He is right.

24
00:04:21,005 --> 00:04:24,005
Begum Hatun is responsible for this treachery.

25
00:04:24,326 --> 00:04:26,685
She got on her horse and went that way.

26
00:04:26,926 --> 00:04:28,725
Sister, what did you do?

27
00:04:29,726 --> 00:04:31,325
Begum Hatun, huh?

28
00:04:33,646 --> 00:04:34,965
So...

29
00:04:35,286 --> 00:04:36,805
Begum Hatun, huh?

30
00:04:40,846 --> 00:04:42,845
Begum Hatun, huh?

31
00:04:44,486 --> 00:04:47,005
I will become her hell.

32
00:04:48,286 --> 00:04:51,805
I will become her hell.

33
00:05:08,366 --> 00:05:09,525
Bala disappeared.

34
00:05:09,566 --> 00:05:12,205
It's like the ground split
open and swallowed her.

35
00:05:12,206 --> 00:05:13,725
But don't worry.

36
00:05:13,726 --> 00:05:15,325
Sofia is also looking for her.

37
00:05:15,326 --> 00:05:18,125
We will surround the forest.
There is no way out for her.

38
00:05:18,126 --> 00:05:19,565
We will find her for sure.

39
00:05:19,926 --> 00:05:22,045
I killed Bala, Ilbay.

40
00:05:28,646 --> 00:05:32,405
-What are you saying, Begum Hatun?
-You heard me. I killed her.

41
00:05:33,286 --> 00:05:35,085
Bala got what she deserved.

42
00:05:39,726 --> 00:05:42,245
Mother!

43
00:05:43,286 --> 00:05:45,525
Mother! What did they do to you?

44
00:05:45,526 --> 00:05:47,845
Mother!

45
00:05:47,846 --> 00:05:50,085
Bala Hatun!

46
00:05:50,086 --> 00:05:52,205
I could not protect you!

47
00:05:52,206 --> 00:05:55,365
I could not help you!

48
00:05:59,166 --> 00:06:00,325
The pain you caused me...

49
00:06:01,566 --> 00:06:04,645
Now your children will suffer
from the same pain, Bala.

50
00:06:05,006 --> 00:06:09,165
Only your children will get hurt, not me.

51
00:06:12,206 --> 00:06:13,885
Mother..

52
00:06:14,526 --> 00:06:17,205
What kind of pain is this, my Allah?

53
00:06:33,806 --> 00:06:36,765
You're the mountain I'm leaning on.

54
00:06:37,326 --> 00:06:42,125
You're my harbor in my hard times. My sun...

55
00:06:42,806 --> 00:06:43,965
..my moon..

56
00:06:44,366 --> 00:06:46,645
...my day and night...

57
00:06:47,446 --> 00:06:49,325
You are my heart.

58
00:06:51,646 --> 00:06:53,725
You were always with me. Always.

59
00:06:53,806 --> 00:06:56,485
Since the day you said yes
to me, when I swung swords...

60
00:06:56,526 --> 00:07:00,765
...and fought the heathens, I
always had you in my mind.

61
00:07:01,126 --> 00:07:03,365
My strong wife...

62
00:07:03,886 --> 00:07:06,525
All burdens feel lighter with you.

63
00:07:06,646 --> 00:07:09,125
You are my prayer which was answered.

64
00:07:21,406 --> 00:07:23,205
Killing Bala was a mistake.

65
00:07:23,686 --> 00:07:24,725
A mistake?

66
00:07:24,726 --> 00:07:26,805
Bala had long deserved to die.

67
00:07:26,806 --> 00:07:28,605
Remember what happened to Osman.

68
00:07:28,606 --> 00:07:30,285
Should I have let her live and escape?

69
00:07:30,286 --> 00:07:33,325
Once we got Osman, they
both would have died anyway.

70
00:07:33,326 --> 00:07:35,285
Now Osman will attack for revenge.

71
00:07:35,286 --> 00:07:39,925
Osman's heart that burns with the grief of
losing Bala will lead him to make mistakes.

72
00:07:40,206 --> 00:07:43,285
Let him attack. We'll be waiting.

73
00:07:43,606 --> 00:07:45,765
Osman was a dead fire, Begum.

74
00:07:46,086 --> 00:07:48,125
He did not have his Alps and people.

75
00:07:48,606 --> 00:07:50,365
Now, you have revived that fire.

76
00:07:50,366 --> 00:07:55,565
Then I will light a fire for Osman
too, and turn him to ashes in that fire.

77
00:07:57,086 --> 00:07:58,405
Begum!

78
00:08:01,246 --> 00:08:05,765
Nokers(Mongolian soldiers), attack!

79
00:08:09,126 --> 00:08:11,965
Stop him!

80
00:08:21,326 --> 00:08:23,245
You will lose anyway Osman!

81
00:08:23,246 --> 00:08:29,245
You martyred my heart,
my Bala, so treacherously...

82
00:08:29,246 --> 00:08:31,965
Now I will burn you in both worlds.

83
00:08:33,246 --> 00:08:35,885
I will send you seven layers below the earth.

84
00:08:36,086 --> 00:08:39,525
I will not find peace until
I gouge out your eyes.

85
00:08:40,486 --> 00:08:43,845
My sword will find peace only with blood.

86
00:08:44,086 --> 00:08:48,125
I will never stop until I take Bala's revenge.

87
00:08:48,126 --> 00:08:50,765
Nokers(Mongolian soldiers)! Attack!

88
00:09:00,446 --> 00:09:02,085
Ilbay...

89
00:09:03,046 --> 00:09:04,245
So...

90
00:09:04,966 --> 00:09:08,445
...they first captured Osman's Hatun...

91
00:09:10,126 --> 00:09:11,485
...then..

92
00:09:11,486 --> 00:09:13,565
...they let her run away, huh?

93
00:09:15,646 --> 00:09:17,885
It's not just her who ran away, Ulugan.

94
00:09:18,206 --> 00:09:21,645
Bala took Cerkutay and his dog from our hands.

95
00:09:26,406 --> 00:09:28,645
Then let's be thankful, Altuga.

96
00:09:32,006 --> 00:09:36,325
Let's be thankful that Osman's
Hatun hasn't taken our sky from above...

97
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:39,805
...and the soil from beneath our feet.

98
00:09:39,806 --> 00:09:42,165
Let's be thankful! -Ulugan!

99
00:09:47,966 --> 00:09:51,125
I will slit your throat, Altuga.

100
00:09:51,366 --> 00:09:54,045
I will clean myself with your blood, Altuga.

101
00:09:54,686 --> 00:09:57,565
You were responsible of the tribe's safety.

102
00:09:58,406 --> 00:10:01,085
Even though Ilbay and Begum made a mistake...

103
00:10:01,086 --> 00:10:03,325
...you were the one who was careless.

104
00:10:12,166 --> 00:10:15,005
Quickly! Go after them!

105
00:10:15,166 --> 00:10:17,125
Go support Ilbay!

106
00:10:17,966 --> 00:10:20,325
Kill Cerkutay and his boy.

107
00:10:20,806 --> 00:10:24,285
But I want Osman's wife alive.

108
00:10:24,846 --> 00:10:26,045
Get lost!

109
00:10:32,886 --> 00:10:35,165
We're here, my Bey!

110
00:10:44,966 --> 00:10:46,165
Are you alright?

111
00:10:46,526 --> 00:10:48,885
Let's get out of here. Come on!

112
00:10:50,286 --> 00:10:51,965
Come on, come on.

113
00:10:52,206 --> 00:10:56,965
There is nothing more enjoyable
than watching Turks fighting each other.

114
00:10:58,046 --> 00:11:01,045
You had ruined my plans, Begum.

115
00:11:01,126 --> 00:11:04,685
Now you have to save your filthy life yourself.

116
00:11:08,606 --> 00:11:10,405
The Righteous!

117
00:11:23,486 --> 00:11:25,685
They're going towards the tribe, my Bey.

118
00:11:25,966 --> 00:11:28,785
There are nokers(Mongolian soldiers)
everywhere, my Bey.

119
00:11:28,886 --> 00:11:31,085
Even if they go through the hell gates,

120
00:11:31,286 --> 00:11:33,005
...they can't run away from me.

121
00:11:33,046 --> 00:11:34,805
As they did this to my Bala,

122
00:11:34,926 --> 00:11:37,045
...they will all die! Come on

123
00:11:46,206 --> 00:11:49,445
My silk-haired mother.

124
00:11:50,846 --> 00:11:53,405
My gazelle-hearted mother.

125
00:11:55,326 --> 00:12:02,445
What have they done to you,
mother? They hurt you badly.

126
00:12:02,966 --> 00:12:09,205
They hurt you, mother. Tell
me. What should I do now?

127
00:12:09,606 --> 00:12:11,485
What should I do?

128
00:12:17,966 --> 00:12:21,645
How many lives should I take...

129
00:12:23,006 --> 00:12:25,845
How many states should I destroy to avenge you?

130
00:12:31,966 --> 00:12:35,165
You would tell me...

131
00:12:36,606 --> 00:12:39,405
...that Allah always shows the way.

132
00:12:40,286 --> 00:12:43,085
Tell me now. What should I do, mother?

133
00:12:57,606 --> 00:13:00,845
Where you don't exist isn't home to me.

134
00:13:02,526 --> 00:13:04,885
Where should I go now, mother?

135
00:13:05,166 --> 00:13:07,965
Where should I go, mother? Where?

136
00:13:13,606 --> 00:13:15,845
The fire touched you...

137
00:13:17,806 --> 00:13:20,645
But it's me who burned to ashes, mother.

138
00:13:22,886 --> 00:13:25,485
Your Alaaddin burned to ashes.

139
00:13:31,766 --> 00:13:34,445
How can I endure this, mother?

140
00:13:35,886 --> 00:13:38,525
How can I endure this?

141
00:14:10,966 --> 00:14:14,805
Trails lead to the tribe, my Bey.

142
00:14:18,566 --> 00:14:21,085
Someone's coming, my Bey. Alps!

143
00:14:24,766 --> 00:14:26,765
It's Cerkutay Bey, my Bey.

144
00:14:27,206 --> 00:14:28,845
My Bey.

145
00:14:31,206 --> 00:14:34,605
My Bey, my Bey.

146
00:14:35,286 --> 00:14:39,125
Bala Hatun isn't in the tribe,
my Bey. We escaped, my Bey.

147
00:14:39,326 --> 00:14:41,205
She's with Ghazi and Meryem.

148
00:14:45,406 --> 00:14:50,405
I split up to to distract those jackals, my Bey.

149
00:14:53,846 --> 00:14:57,365
My Bey... My Bey.

150
00:14:57,926 --> 00:15:00,045
Bala Hatun is safe.

151
00:15:00,406 --> 00:15:02,005
Cerkutay Bey.

152
00:15:03,166 --> 00:15:04,805
Mother Bala...

153
00:15:07,126 --> 00:15:08,765
My mother...

154
00:15:14,526 --> 00:15:16,325
...passed away.

155
00:15:20,686 --> 00:15:22,525
No, no.

156
00:15:22,646 --> 00:15:24,885
No, my Shahzade.

157
00:15:27,646 --> 00:15:30,285
What is my Shahzade talking about, my Bey?

158
00:15:35,606 --> 00:15:38,125
Couldn't I protect her?

159
00:15:40,526 --> 00:15:43,805
I couldn't protect... Bala Hatun...Ghazi.

160
00:15:44,526 --> 00:15:46,525
Couldn't I protect Ghazi?

161
00:15:46,806 --> 00:15:48,805
Don't worry, Cerkutay.

162
00:15:49,366 --> 00:15:52,045
Ghazi is alive. He's alright.

163
00:15:56,646 --> 00:15:59,085
I disappointed my Bey.

164
00:16:01,966 --> 00:16:05,346
-Even if Begum Hatun goes to the tribe,
I'll cut off her head!

165
00:16:05,346 --> 00:16:07,206
My Bey, nokers are standing on alert!

166
00:16:07,206 --> 00:16:08,885
Get out of my way, Cerkutay!

167
00:16:09,206 --> 00:16:10,725
My Bey.

168
00:16:13,486 --> 00:16:17,765
-My Bey, no! I can't let you go! Please!
-Cerkutay!

169
00:16:18,326 --> 00:16:23,085
You both disobey me and
stop me from finding Bala's killer!

170
00:16:43,246 --> 00:16:45,845
It's my fault. I couldn't...

171
00:16:46,206 --> 00:16:47,885
I couldn't protect.

172
00:16:48,006 --> 00:16:50,605
It's my fault.

173
00:16:51,846 --> 00:16:55,405
It's my fault. My fault!

174
00:16:55,886 --> 00:16:57,965
You go join Alaaddin.

175
00:16:58,846 --> 00:17:01,405
I'll go after my father.

176
00:17:02,206 --> 00:17:07,085
-It's my fault. I couldn't...
-Cerkutay.

177
00:17:08,046 --> 00:17:09,723
Cerkutay.

178
00:17:10,646 --> 00:17:14,165
Come on, brother. Pull yourself together.

179
00:17:47,486 --> 00:17:51,085
I couldn't protect her.

180
00:17:59,406 --> 00:18:01,325
It's my fault.

181
00:18:02,326 --> 00:18:04,445
It's not your fault.

182
00:18:05,286 --> 00:18:07,445
It was my traitor sister.

183
00:18:07,766 --> 00:18:11,085
Don't blame yourself,
Cerkutay Bey. It's not your fault.

184
00:18:11,406 --> 00:18:14,205
Cerkutay Bey, I know it hurts.

185
00:18:14,646 --> 00:18:16,365
I know the feeling.

186
00:18:16,846 --> 00:18:18,645
But it's not your fault.

187
00:18:18,846 --> 00:18:21,005
Don't be upset.

188
00:18:25,406 --> 00:18:27,765
By rising against those blood suckers

189
00:18:27,886 --> 00:18:30,365
...you did your part, Cerkutay Bey.

190
00:18:34,966 --> 00:18:39,005
I wish my Bey had killed me.

191
00:18:39,086 --> 00:18:41,125
I don't deserve to live.

192
00:18:41,286 --> 00:18:46,365
I don't deserve to live. Get off! Get off!

193
00:18:47,686 --> 00:18:49,685
Don't you hear me?

194
00:18:50,046 --> 00:18:51,965
Don't you see?

195
00:18:52,646 --> 00:18:54,405
It is my fault.

196
00:18:54,766 --> 00:18:57,725
-I couldn't protect her!
-Cerkutay!

197
00:18:58,526 --> 00:19:00,885
Cerkutay, my brother.

198
00:19:01,326 --> 00:19:03,605
Pull yourself together. Enough!

199
00:19:03,926 --> 00:19:05,685
What are you even saying?

200
00:19:05,806 --> 00:19:09,885
I'm saying the right thing.
Saying the right thing!

201
00:19:12,646 --> 00:19:15,925
I say it's not your fault. Don't you get it?

202
00:19:18,406 --> 00:19:19,765
Brother.

203
00:19:20,166 --> 00:19:22,045
Brother.

204
00:19:22,286 --> 00:19:25,485
-How can I even talk to my Bey again?
-Brother.

205
00:19:26,046 --> 00:19:28,405
Cerkutay, my brother.

206
00:19:28,406 --> 00:19:32,605
-How can I even stand beside him again?
-Cerkutay!

207
00:19:32,686 --> 00:19:34,685
Cerkutay, my brother.

208
00:19:34,926 --> 00:19:36,085
Brother.

209
00:19:37,246 --> 00:19:38,925
Cerkutay, it's the death.

210
00:19:39,606 --> 00:19:41,645
It's the death, brother.

211
00:19:42,486 --> 00:19:45,005
Who can even stand against the death?

212
00:19:45,646 --> 00:19:50,485
Brother, a mortal pen
can't write a person's fate.

213
00:19:50,606 --> 00:19:52,285
It can't.

214
00:19:54,366 --> 00:19:56,525
It's only Allah Who decides, brother.

215
00:19:57,606 --> 00:20:01,765
Pull yourself together. We need to
go now. Pull yourself together, brother.

216
00:20:02,166 --> 00:20:05,205
-It's only Allah Who decides.
-Yes, brother.

217
00:20:05,206 --> 00:20:07,285
Come on, let's go.

218
00:20:09,926 --> 00:20:12,645
Come on, brother. Let's go, alps!

219
00:20:12,726 --> 00:20:13,965
Come on.

220
00:20:14,406 --> 00:20:15,965
My Shahzade.

221
00:20:16,886 --> 00:20:19,925
My Shahzade... My Shahzade...

222
00:20:21,246 --> 00:20:23,485
I wish I had died instead!

223
00:20:24,086 --> 00:20:26,525
I wish!

224
00:20:27,246 --> 00:20:31,405
I wish I were lying down there instead of Bala!

225
00:20:32,726 --> 00:20:35,725
I wish I had died! Not Mother Bala!

226
00:20:37,326 --> 00:20:41,765
I wish I had died instead of Mother Bala!

227
00:20:42,646 --> 00:20:44,805
No more dying, Ghazi.

228
00:20:47,166 --> 00:20:49,205
We will avenge.

229
00:20:56,086 --> 00:20:58,365
We will have our grief.

230
00:21:00,606 --> 00:21:02,485
We will have it, but...

231
00:21:46,486 --> 00:21:48,725
My Shahzade.

232
00:22:10,726 --> 00:22:13,085
The snake called Begum has run off.

233
00:22:18,926 --> 00:22:20,965
Where is Osman Bey?

234
00:22:21,606 --> 00:22:23,125
My Bey's gone.

235
00:22:24,206 --> 00:22:26,125
He was acting weirdly.

236
00:22:26,846 --> 00:22:30,005
We don't know where he's
gone or what he's going to do.

237
00:22:30,686 --> 00:22:34,165
Boran Bey has gone after him just in case.

238
00:22:35,926 --> 00:22:37,485
Fine.

239
00:22:41,766 --> 00:22:43,485
Now..

240
00:22:48,446 --> 00:22:50,645
We're going to Sogut.

241
00:22:51,326 --> 00:22:53,405
Okay, my Shahzade.

242
00:23:23,686 --> 00:23:28,365
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate. Don't. Don't.

243
00:23:31,006 --> 00:23:32,965
Nobody will touch her.

244
00:23:35,086 --> 00:23:37,125
I will carry my mother.

245
00:23:40,286 --> 00:23:42,365
I will carry her.

246
00:24:03,886 --> 00:24:08,165
Dastards. Dastards.

247
00:24:11,366 --> 00:24:13,525
You hurt me.

248
00:24:13,886 --> 00:24:16,245
You hurt my heart.

249
00:24:16,726 --> 00:24:20,685
You didn't only take Bala from me..

250
00:24:21,366 --> 00:24:23,525
...but also all my mercy.

251
00:24:23,806 --> 00:24:30,085
What I'm going to do to you
will spread all around the world!

252
00:24:32,926 --> 00:24:35,645
My Bey.
-Son.

253
00:24:44,326 --> 00:24:46,445
No walls..

254
00:24:47,126 --> 00:24:51,685
No shields can stop us from avenging my mother.

255
00:24:53,886 --> 00:24:57,205
But, my Bey... Now...

256
00:24:58,646 --> 00:25:01,605
Now it's time to mourn.

257
00:25:03,086 --> 00:25:05,685
We mourn not by waiting...

258
00:25:06,606 --> 00:25:10,725
...but by vengeance and blood.

259
00:25:34,926 --> 00:25:36,605
You called us here Ulugan.

260
00:25:54,286 --> 00:25:57,365
What do you think you are doing to my Hatun?
-Shut up!

261
00:26:06,966 --> 00:26:11,085
What did you do behind my back, huh?

262
00:26:11,966 --> 00:26:14,485
How did you kill a prisoner...

263
00:26:15,166 --> 00:26:18,285
...under my control? How dare you?

264
00:26:20,366 --> 00:26:23,485
We keep making plans.

265
00:26:23,486 --> 00:26:26,885
We keep making moves,
but we cannot move forward.

266
00:26:26,966 --> 00:26:28,965
I did what needed to be done.

267
00:26:29,126 --> 00:26:31,445
I left Osman helpless.

268
00:26:31,726 --> 00:26:35,365
If there was a man among
you, he would do what I did.

269
00:26:35,366 --> 00:26:37,245
Hatun.

270
00:26:38,646 --> 00:26:40,845
Your hair is long...

271
00:26:41,206 --> 00:26:43,125
...but your mind is short.

272
00:26:44,126 --> 00:26:46,525
You didn't defeat Osman.

273
00:26:46,566 --> 00:26:48,445
You made him more aggressive.

274
00:26:50,086 --> 00:26:52,165
Let him do all he can.

275
00:26:52,486 --> 00:26:53,845
We are here.

276
00:26:54,966 --> 00:26:58,205
You act with the mind of your Hatun.

277
00:26:58,686 --> 00:27:00,805
But let me give you an advice.

278
00:27:00,806 --> 00:27:04,045
What burns quickly burns out quickly.

279
00:27:04,686 --> 00:27:06,965
Osman is a wounded wolf.

280
00:27:06,966 --> 00:27:11,845
A wounded wolf doesn't care about the
hunter behind him or the pain he will feel.

281
00:27:13,366 --> 00:27:16,965
Osman will attack us. He will attack the tribe.

282
00:27:18,406 --> 00:27:21,485
Osman was going to attack
the tribe sooner or later.

283
00:27:21,606 --> 00:27:23,725
He can come, we will resist.

284
00:27:24,206 --> 00:27:25,525
you..

285
00:27:26,886 --> 00:27:30,765
...make a move without informing me again...

286
00:27:31,766 --> 00:27:35,045
...I will take your head before Osman does.

287
00:27:36,046 --> 00:27:37,965
Then what do we have to do?

288
00:27:46,806 --> 00:27:48,165
It's my order.

289
00:27:48,966 --> 00:27:56,325
All the nokers, all your Alps, and even
Sofia's Byzantine soldiers will gather.

290
00:27:57,886 --> 00:28:01,805
If Osman started the war, we will win.

291
00:28:20,886 --> 00:28:26,365
If I am Begum Hatun, just like I took
my revenge from Bala for that slap...

292
00:28:26,406 --> 00:28:29,205
...I will take revenge
from Ulugan as well, Ilbay!

293
00:28:39,526 --> 00:28:41,565
Mother!

294
00:28:41,566 --> 00:28:42,565
Ghazi!

295
00:28:46,446 --> 00:28:47,885
My dear!

296
00:28:48,526 --> 00:28:50,765
Welcome... welcome...

297
00:28:52,006 --> 00:28:53,525
Mother..

298
00:28:54,406 --> 00:28:56,365
They killed Bala Hatun, mother.

299
00:29:04,566 --> 00:29:05,845
What did you say?

300
00:29:07,046 --> 00:29:08,245
Ghazi?

301
00:29:08,526 --> 00:29:09,765
What did you say?

302
00:29:09,766 --> 00:29:11,405
Ghazi, where is my mother?

303
00:29:12,606 --> 00:29:13,845
Ghazi...

304
00:29:14,526 --> 00:29:15,605
What happened?

305
00:29:15,606 --> 00:29:17,445
Is my mother hurt? What happened?

306
00:29:18,166 --> 00:29:19,245
She burned her.

307
00:29:19,606 --> 00:29:22,045
Begum Hatun burned her alive, Gonca Hatun.

308
00:30:07,886 --> 00:30:09,005
No...

309
00:30:19,806 --> 00:30:20,845
Brother?

310
00:30:46,966 --> 00:30:48,885
My Allah...

311
00:30:56,486 --> 00:30:57,645
Mother..

312
00:31:00,686 --> 00:31:03,085
Was this our fate, mother?

313
00:31:14,366 --> 00:31:17,125
In the name of Allah,
the merciful, the compassionate.

314
00:31:40,046 --> 00:31:41,685
Bala Hatun!

315
00:31:51,726 --> 00:31:52,805
Brother..

316
00:31:53,926 --> 00:31:59,045
Brother... No..
No... Brother..

317
00:31:59,046 --> 00:32:00,405
What is this, brother?

318
00:32:00,526 --> 00:32:03,485
Brother, tell me it's not real. Brother!

319
00:32:03,606 --> 00:32:04,805
Sister...

320
00:32:04,806 --> 00:32:07,485
Brother, no, no, tell me it is not real!

321
00:32:07,486 --> 00:32:09,605
Tell me it's not real... It's not my mother!

322
00:32:09,606 --> 00:32:12,885
No, it's not my mother! It's not!

323
00:32:16,006 --> 00:32:17,725
My Fatma, it's our mother...

324
00:32:21,126 --> 00:32:24,165
No... No... No, no!

325
00:32:24,166 --> 00:32:27,365
No... I'll look! I ll look!

326
00:32:27,366 --> 00:32:30,285
No, don't, Fatma. Don't!

327
00:32:34,966 --> 00:32:36,645
Brother...

328
00:32:38,726 --> 00:32:41,165
Her hand, brother... Her hand, brother!

329
00:32:41,166 --> 00:32:45,845
Brother! Brother!

330
00:32:45,846 --> 00:32:48,365
Her hand!

331
00:32:53,166 --> 00:32:56,565
No, no! Brother!

332
00:32:59,606 --> 00:33:01,885
Brother, no!

333
00:33:13,406 --> 00:33:15,365
No!

334
00:33:17,766 --> 00:33:19,645
No!

335
00:33:22,766 --> 00:33:24,725
No!

336
00:33:26,046 --> 00:33:28,445
In the name of Allah, the merciful,
the compassionate.

337
00:33:32,166 --> 00:33:34,685
Mother!

338
00:33:35,486 --> 00:33:39,965
My mother is gone... My mother is gone!

339
00:33:52,206 --> 00:33:54,005
O, people!

340
00:33:59,606 --> 00:34:01,565
Sheikh Edebali's daughter...

341
00:34:03,766 --> 00:34:05,845
...Osman Bey's Hatun...

342
00:34:06,926 --> 00:34:10,045
...the glorious mother of all Kayi

343
00:34:14,726 --> 00:34:15,885
My mother...

344
00:34:18,525 --> 00:34:20,125
...Bala Hatun...

345
00:34:22,485 --> 00:34:24,205
...fell a martyr!

346
00:34:25,966 --> 00:34:27,965
Alright, Fatma.

347
00:34:30,485 --> 00:34:32,284
Indeed we belong to Allah...

348
00:34:33,806 --> 00:34:36,205
...and indeed to Him we will return.

349
00:34:39,565 --> 00:34:42,005
Mother!

350
00:35:08,246 --> 00:35:09,325
My Bey...

351
00:35:13,726 --> 00:35:14,885
It's...

352
00:35:19,166 --> 00:35:20,765
...it's my mother's sala.

353
00:35:46,526 --> 00:35:49,045
Brother... -Sister...

354
00:35:49,046 --> 00:35:51,965
Mother! Mother...

355
00:35:51,966 --> 00:35:54,765
Mother!

356
00:35:54,766 --> 00:35:56,005
No...

357
00:36:11,366 --> 00:36:14,085
Mother... mother, come back to me!

358
00:36:14,086 --> 00:36:15,205
Mother, come back!

359
00:36:15,206 --> 00:36:18,205
Brother, save my mother!

360
00:36:18,206 --> 00:36:21,965
Mother..

361
00:36:22,966 --> 00:36:26,205
My heart is burning in flames, brother!

362
00:36:29,366 --> 00:36:31,845
Fatma... Fatma...

363
00:36:37,566 --> 00:36:40,565
My mother is gone... She is gone!

364
00:36:45,486 --> 00:36:48,805
I know sister... I know.

365
00:36:49,806 --> 00:36:51,485
I know.

366
00:36:54,046 --> 00:36:57,845
It will be alright, my Fatma.

367
00:37:06,286 --> 00:37:09,605
It will be alright. -Brother...

368
00:37:12,886 --> 00:37:16,845
It will be alright.. My beautiful sister...

369
00:37:16,846 --> 00:37:18,845
My dear...

370
00:37:21,926 --> 00:37:24,485
Gonca. Holofira.

371
00:37:34,566 --> 00:37:36,845
It will be alright, dear...

372
00:37:37,046 --> 00:37:39,285
You will be alright.

373
00:37:40,286 --> 00:37:42,765
You will be alright.

374
00:37:43,806 --> 00:37:45,165
This sorrow..

375
00:37:46,686 --> 00:37:48,845
...this pain destroyed us all.

376
00:37:53,326 --> 00:37:55,685
It left us helpless!

377
00:37:57,406 --> 00:37:58,525
Today...

378
00:38:00,166 --> 00:38:02,565
...is the day of grief for Kayi, people!

379
00:38:05,006 --> 00:38:06,205
Now...

380
00:38:09,966 --> 00:38:12,445
...it's time for Kayis to mourn.

381
00:38:20,166 --> 00:38:22,165
Get ready for the burial.

382
00:38:23,366 --> 00:38:24,845
Once my father comes...

383
00:38:27,526 --> 00:38:29,365
...we will bury my mother.

384
00:38:30,846 --> 00:38:32,605
We will not bury her!

385
00:38:35,006 --> 00:38:37,565
Osman Bey is here.

386
00:39:07,126 --> 00:39:08,925
Father...

387
00:39:16,646 --> 00:39:18,645
Father...

388
00:39:24,526 --> 00:39:26,485
Fatma..
Father..

389
00:39:39,966 --> 00:39:41,565
Come on, my beautiful daughter.

390
00:41:13,726 --> 00:41:15,525
Until we take our tribe back...

391
00:41:18,846 --> 00:41:21,205
...we will not bury Bala Hatun.

392
00:41:24,926 --> 00:41:26,325
I will not keep her away...

393
00:41:28,966 --> 00:41:30,325
...from her tribe...

394
00:41:32,366 --> 00:41:33,845
...from her tent..

395
00:41:38,366 --> 00:41:41,085
...from her people and her daughter.

396
00:41:43,446 --> 00:41:47,125
I will say this only once.

397
00:41:49,126 --> 00:41:50,805
And until then..

398
00:41:53,446 --> 00:41:54,685
...until Bala Hatun...

399
00:41:56,886 --> 00:41:59,925
...is buried in the land
where her child rests...

400
00:41:59,926 --> 00:42:03,645
...we will never stop!

401
00:42:29,126 --> 00:42:30,205
Come on!

402
00:42:41,566 --> 00:42:42,645
Walk!

403
00:42:44,646 --> 00:42:46,525
Osman and you...

404
00:42:48,366 --> 00:42:52,445
...will die knowing that
you are nothing before me.

405
00:42:55,246 --> 00:42:56,285
Come on!

406
00:43:05,126 --> 00:43:06,725
All this time...

407
00:43:07,766 --> 00:43:10,365
...I've waited only for this.

408
00:43:13,686 --> 00:43:14,725
Come on!

409
00:43:22,126 --> 00:43:24,165
Get up!

410
00:43:50,046 --> 00:43:54,125
The Kayi's fate is set with sorrow!

411
00:43:54,766 --> 00:43:59,165
The ground threw up killers and
swallowed Bala Hatun instead.

412
00:43:59,326 --> 00:44:03,005
-Our hearts are burned with grief!
-My Allah, what should we do now?

413
00:44:06,246 --> 00:44:09,045
Bala Hatun has gone to heaven.

414
00:44:09,046 --> 00:44:12,085
The cruel are ruling the world!

415
00:44:12,766 --> 00:44:14,245
Shut up!

416
00:44:14,686 --> 00:44:16,005
Shut up

417
00:44:17,686 --> 00:44:22,445
In this tribe, nobody will lament for Bala!

418
00:44:22,446 --> 00:44:23,805
Go away!

419
00:44:24,246 --> 00:44:26,765
-Dastards!
-Vile dogs!

420
00:44:26,886 --> 00:44:28,805
You have no mercy!

421
00:44:29,046 --> 00:44:31,085
Cruel

422
00:44:32,686 --> 00:44:38,645
Whoever can't accept the
endless power of Mongolians...

423
00:44:40,086 --> 00:44:43,285
..will die!

424
00:44:45,126 --> 00:44:49,005
Now go back to your tents.

425
00:44:49,806 --> 00:44:54,285
Or I will bury all of you with Osman's wife!

426
00:44:55,806 --> 00:44:58,805
Osman Bey will make you pay for this.

427
00:45:03,606 --> 00:45:07,885
You think Osman will take revenge? You think so?

428
00:45:08,206 --> 00:45:11,245
I'll take off his mourning heart...

429
00:45:11,486 --> 00:45:14,325
...and make you people eat it!

430
00:45:14,806 --> 00:45:16,685
Dastards!

431
00:45:17,086 --> 00:45:18,605
Vile dogs!

432
00:45:18,806 --> 00:45:22,165
Nokers(Mongolian soldiers) show no mercy!

433
00:45:28,966 --> 00:45:30,805
Leave us!

434
00:45:31,246 --> 00:45:35,085
Dastards!

435
00:47:41,686 --> 00:47:43,605
My Bala.

436
00:47:53,206 --> 00:47:56,085
I knew you wouldn't leave me.

437
00:48:00,766 --> 00:48:02,685
I knew it.

438
00:48:03,766 --> 00:48:05,765
Bala..

439
00:48:53,566 --> 00:48:55,805
Bala..

440
00:49:01,246 --> 00:49:03,205
Bala...

441
00:49:24,366 --> 00:49:27,525
We shouldn't have got separated like this.

442
00:49:32,966 --> 00:49:35,885
We shouldn't have got separated like this.

443
00:50:00,206 --> 00:50:03,445
I shouldn't have come to this tree alone.

444
00:50:04,246 --> 00:50:07,885
I should have passed away before you.

445
00:50:21,606 --> 00:50:23,365
Bala.

446
00:50:29,966 --> 00:50:32,445
Bala.

447
00:50:33,246 --> 00:50:38,125
You devil! Sofia, what's your plan?

448
00:50:38,526 --> 00:50:40,805
-Where are you taking me?
-Move!

449
00:50:41,046 --> 00:50:43,405
Why didn't you leave me?

450
00:50:44,126 --> 00:50:47,845
I'll make you face the hell! I
will make you face the hell!

451
00:50:53,126 --> 00:50:57,805
If I hadn't saved you,
you'd have faced the hell!

452
00:50:59,566 --> 00:51:02,805
You should thank me, shouldn't you?

453
00:51:24,366 --> 00:51:26,325
Poena.

454
00:51:27,886 --> 00:51:29,365
Aunt.

455
00:51:29,606 --> 00:51:32,005
Begum burned the cabin.

456
00:51:35,086 --> 00:51:37,165
Stupid Begum.

457
00:51:38,246 --> 00:51:41,525
How can you stop Osman if you kill Bala?

458
00:51:41,926 --> 00:51:43,365
Stupid!

459
00:51:45,046 --> 00:51:47,805
Bala is burning...

460
00:51:50,086 --> 00:51:52,125
She's dying, aunt.

461
00:51:55,086 --> 00:51:57,485
I won't let her die for now.

462
00:51:57,606 --> 00:52:00,445
If she dies, we can't catch Osman.

463
00:52:15,006 --> 00:52:17,045
Poena, come here!

464
00:52:19,286 --> 00:52:21,245
Take off her clothes.

465
00:52:21,486 --> 00:52:25,645
-Why?
-Hurry up. Poena. Don't ask questions.

466
00:52:33,846 --> 00:52:35,485
Bala!

467
00:52:39,806 --> 00:52:43,285
Bala, come! Come

468
00:52:44,126 --> 00:52:45,525
Come!

469
00:52:53,526 --> 00:52:56,205
I want you to die so much, Bala!

470
00:52:58,366 --> 00:53:00,165
But not now.

471
00:53:01,126 --> 00:53:03,125
Vengeance first.

472
00:53:05,846 --> 00:53:07,645
Bala.

473
00:53:09,086 --> 00:53:12,165
No, Bala. You can't die now.

474
00:53:12,246 --> 00:53:15,165
Bala! Bala!

475
00:53:15,846 --> 00:53:18,285
Bala! Bala?

476
00:53:30,326 --> 00:53:32,285
Sofia.

477
00:53:34,086 --> 00:53:36,805
You owe me a life.

478
00:53:43,486 --> 00:53:44,445
Look.

479
00:53:44,646 --> 00:53:47,605
We'll make Bala put on these.

480
00:53:47,766 --> 00:53:50,085
And make the girl put on Bala's clothes.

481
00:53:51,286 --> 00:53:54,485
-Why?
-To kill Bala.

482
00:53:56,926 --> 00:54:00,205
-They'll think Bala is dead.
-Good, little bird.

483
00:54:00,846 --> 00:54:02,685
Good. Yes.

484
00:54:11,126 --> 00:54:12,765
Come on.

485
00:54:19,326 --> 00:54:21,325
Here.

486
00:54:29,286 --> 00:54:32,925
Poena, go hide.

487
00:54:33,366 --> 00:54:36,885
When Osman comes, tell him Bala is dead.

488
00:54:38,086 --> 00:54:40,325
And blame Begum.

489
00:54:41,766 --> 00:54:46,405
What is your evil plan, huh?
What are you intending to do?

490
00:54:46,726 --> 00:54:49,325
Why didn't you let me die there?

491
00:54:49,686 --> 00:54:51,045
What do you want?

492
00:54:54,046 --> 00:54:56,245
You can't die so easily, Bala.

493
00:54:57,766 --> 00:55:01,845
You haven't tasted the most bitter
grief yet that I prepared for you.

494
00:55:04,806 --> 00:55:06,845
Besides, I'd never let you...

495
00:55:08,606 --> 00:55:10,525
...die without Osman.

496
00:55:10,966 --> 00:55:13,125
I'll kill you myself.

497
00:55:13,406 --> 00:55:15,605
I'll kill you in such a way...

498
00:55:15,686 --> 00:55:17,645
...that you won't be able to escape.

499
00:55:17,766 --> 00:55:20,605
Stop having false hopes, Bala.

500
00:55:25,806 --> 00:55:30,925
Finding out that you're alive,
Osman will fall into my hands.

501
00:55:31,806 --> 00:55:34,965
And I will take unprecedented revenge...

502
00:55:36,806 --> 00:55:38,645
...from you people.

503
00:55:39,126 --> 00:55:41,405
Just a little patience.

504
00:55:42,086 --> 00:55:43,765
Patience.

505
00:55:53,686 --> 00:55:56,205
We still had time.

506
00:55:58,486 --> 00:56:03,245
I should have left this world before you.

507
00:56:11,726 --> 00:56:16,565
Bala. Bala...

508
00:56:19,726 --> 00:56:23,045
They think I'm a tree.

509
00:56:23,726 --> 00:56:25,485
Like this plane tree.

510
00:56:26,126 --> 00:56:34,085
They think I'm a mountain
like those high mountains.

511
00:56:34,966 --> 00:56:40,885
But that mountain was
holding on to another mountain.

512
00:56:42,846 --> 00:56:45,325
You were my mountain.

513
00:56:47,646 --> 00:56:52,245
But the dark mountain has just collapsed.

514
00:56:52,926 --> 00:56:55,845
The strong tree got cut.

515
00:56:56,926 --> 00:57:01,645
My sturdy chest got pierced.

516
00:57:03,046 --> 00:57:07,605
The light enlightening the
dark in my eyes has just died.

517
00:57:12,726 --> 00:57:16,765
It has just died.

518
00:57:17,206 --> 00:57:20,405
It has just died.

519
00:57:20,766 --> 00:57:24,645
It has just died.

520
00:57:34,486 --> 00:57:36,445
Move!

521
00:58:18,686 --> 00:58:21,005
Oh, son..

522
00:58:25,966 --> 00:58:27,965
It's getting dark, father.

523
00:58:28,846 --> 00:58:30,845
It's time for dinner.

524
00:58:31,526 --> 00:58:33,845
Without my mother, though.

525
00:58:35,566 --> 00:58:39,205
Without her voice and smell...

526
00:58:40,566 --> 00:58:42,725
Without mother's wings, father.

527
00:58:43,286 --> 00:58:46,965
Your mother is like a phoenix.

528
00:58:47,326 --> 00:58:49,765
She'll rise from the ashes.

529
00:58:50,046 --> 00:58:52,605
Don't worry. Look.

530
00:58:54,006 --> 00:58:58,245
Just right here. Right here.

531
00:59:03,006 --> 00:59:08,045
How can we endure this suffering, father?

532
00:59:08,206 --> 00:59:10,165
Well..

533
00:59:10,726 --> 00:59:12,685
First, we lost my sister.

534
00:59:15,046 --> 00:59:17,485
Then we lost my unborn baby.

535
00:59:19,686 --> 00:59:21,565
And now mother.

536
00:59:23,166 --> 00:59:27,045
It's like I lose whatever I hold on to.

537
00:59:27,646 --> 00:59:31,605
Son, you should hold on to your cause.

538
00:59:32,166 --> 00:59:34,165
Hold on to your love.

539
00:59:34,726 --> 00:59:36,645
Hold on to life.

540
00:59:37,406 --> 00:59:38,925
Look at me.

541
00:59:39,446 --> 00:59:41,525
We'll avenge your mother.

542
00:59:42,086 --> 00:59:43,685
We will, father.

543
01:00:08,966 --> 01:00:10,605
Move aside!

544
01:00:12,966 --> 01:00:15,845
My lady, Begum Hatun killed Bala...

545
01:00:25,606 --> 01:00:29,725
-Put her in the darkest dungeon.
-Yes, my lady!

546
01:00:33,566 --> 01:00:35,765
Chain her arms and legs!

547
01:00:37,326 --> 01:00:39,925
My lady, everybody thinks Bala is dead.

548
01:00:40,726 --> 01:00:42,765
Because I wanted so.

549
01:00:43,126 --> 01:00:47,085
Osman should burn with
suffering and make a mistake.

550
01:00:47,646 --> 01:00:52,285
Then birds will whisper
to him that Bala is alive.

551
01:00:52,406 --> 01:00:57,925
And Osman will come to his death himself.

552
01:00:59,246 --> 01:01:02,965
What about Ulugan?
Does he know that Bala is...

553
01:01:05,126 --> 01:01:09,405
Whoever isn't loyal to me doesn't know.

554
01:01:15,446 --> 01:01:17,205
And nobody will know.

555
01:01:17,686 --> 01:01:19,045
Uluga

556
01:01:19,406 --> 01:01:22,005
...wants our soldiers to join his nokers.

557
01:01:22,206 --> 01:01:24,365
What do you order about this?

558
01:01:25,686 --> 01:01:29,725
Osman will be overwhelmed by
grief for Bala and attack the tribe.

559
01:01:31,286 --> 01:01:33,845
There will both nokers and us.

560
01:01:34,326 --> 01:01:37,005
So Osman won't be able to run off.

561
01:01:37,606 --> 01:01:42,045
Prepare soldiers immediately
and make them join Ulugan.

562
01:01:43,526 --> 01:01:47,925
I will take his last hope from Osman...

563
01:01:50,246 --> 01:01:56,245
...and play cat and mouse with him.

564
01:02:03,006 --> 01:02:04,765
My Bey.

565
01:02:05,646 --> 01:02:07,805
.we've got the news

566
01:02:08,486 --> 01:02:13,645
...that Byzantine soldiers arrived in
the tribe and joined Ulugan's nokers.

567
01:02:16,726 --> 01:02:19,365
Heathens know...

568
01:02:21,246 --> 01:02:26,165
...Kayis won't stop as Bala Hatun's gone.

569
01:02:27,406 --> 01:02:33,285
They'll look for a corpse to bite off!

570
01:02:36,486 --> 01:02:39,765
Well... What's the situation?

571
01:02:39,846 --> 01:02:45,925
We united our alps in captivity in Sogut
and the alps Yusuf Bey made join us.

572
01:02:46,406 --> 01:02:50,445
All of them are ready to fight now, my Bey.

573
01:02:50,686 --> 01:02:55,445
With the ones we seized in
Sogut, we lack no weapons, my Bey.

574
01:02:55,846 --> 01:03:01,205
You should just give one order for us to
take back the tribe and avenge my mother.

575
01:03:01,566 --> 01:03:03,405
We are ready.

576
01:03:09,886 --> 01:03:16,085
This wild fire burning in our chests...

577
01:03:19,166 --> 01:03:21,725
...is ready for vengeance.

578
01:03:25,526 --> 01:03:27,405
But...

579
01:03:29,646 --> 01:03:36,085
We're outnumbered by
heathens. They are stronger now.

580
01:03:36,446 --> 01:03:39,165
I was going to mention that, my Bey.

581
01:03:39,766 --> 01:03:44,005
How about we wait for some
time to gain more strength?

582
01:03:45,486 --> 01:03:47,725
What are you talking about, Yusuf?

583
01:03:52,246 --> 01:03:57,605
When we performed the
ritual for Bala Hatun outside

584
01:03:57,846 --> 01:04:02,205
...didn't I say that we would never stop?

585
01:04:04,806 --> 01:04:12,085
Before we take back our
tribe and bury Bala Hatun,

586
01:04:14,006 --> 01:04:16,725
...we will never stop.

587
01:04:17,566 --> 01:04:22,845
Even if they are a thousand times
as many as us, we will never stop!

588
01:04:31,406 --> 01:04:33,445
Well..

589
01:04:35,326 --> 01:04:37,325
What bothers me is...

590
01:04:37,686 --> 01:04:40,805
When we want to attack the tribe

591
01:04:41,686 --> 01:04:46,125
...they will try to ambush
us before we reach there.

592
01:04:47,486 --> 01:04:50,645
As we have such a powerful enemy.

593
01:04:53,246 --> 01:04:55,285
...we should be prepared.

594
01:04:56,126 --> 01:04:58,525
Listen carefully now.

595
01:05:17,846 --> 01:05:20,165
Osman is getting ready, Ulugan.

596
01:05:20,526 --> 01:05:22,325
Just as you thought...

597
01:05:22,566 --> 01:05:25,805
Apparently, he will attack the tribe tomorrow.

598
01:05:26,366 --> 01:05:28,205
We need to act fast.

599
01:05:38,086 --> 01:05:41,965
Being fast is for horses.

600
01:05:44,006 --> 01:05:47,725
An eagle waits for the right time.

601
01:05:52,006 --> 01:05:55,445
Are my nokers(Mongolian soldiers) ready, Altuga?

602
01:05:56,366 --> 01:05:58,885
They are all ready to fight, Ulugan.

603
01:05:59,526 --> 01:06:02,565
Our shouts will shake the battlefield.

604
01:06:07,246 --> 01:06:08,845
What about the Byzantines?

605
01:06:09,086 --> 01:06:11,485
Sofia sent all the forces she had.

606
01:06:11,806 --> 01:06:13,645
They are waiting for your order.

607
01:06:17,206 --> 01:06:18,285
Good.

608
01:06:21,606 --> 01:06:25,005
A wolf does not fear an ambush, but...

609
01:06:26,726 --> 01:06:28,965
...it pays its price with its life.

610
01:06:31,166 --> 01:06:34,205
I will cut you into forty pieces, Osman.

611
01:06:37,126 --> 01:06:38,485
Altuga...

612
01:06:39,926 --> 01:06:45,525
At sunrise, you and I will head towards Sogut.

613
01:06:46,206 --> 01:06:51,325
Before Osman reaches the
tribe, we will destroy Sogut.

614
01:06:52,646 --> 01:06:53,965
Then...

615
01:06:55,126 --> 01:06:58,925
We will take Sogut back.

616
01:07:01,486 --> 01:07:02,645
Ilbay...

617
01:07:04,086 --> 01:07:06,125
You will stay here.

618
01:07:06,646 --> 01:07:11,765
If anyone gets past us,
you will protect the tribe.

619
01:07:11,766 --> 01:07:13,885
I will be a shield with my Alps, Ulugan.

620
01:07:14,606 --> 01:07:16,005
Do not worry.

621
01:07:16,006 --> 01:07:18,005
Not only with your Alps...

622
01:07:18,766 --> 01:07:22,405
...you will use all of
Osman's people as a shield.

623
01:07:22,406 --> 01:07:27,365
Tie everyone, children and all, to
stakes and place them on the road.

624
01:07:28,846 --> 01:07:30,165
Do it...

625
01:07:32,926 --> 01:07:35,405
...so Osman cannot shoot arrows...

626
01:07:36,326 --> 01:07:38,445
...or ride his horse.

627
01:07:39,286 --> 01:07:41,605
I will protect the tribe in such a way that...

628
01:07:42,366 --> 01:07:44,645
...Osman will not make a single move.

629
01:07:45,446 --> 01:07:47,325
Do not worry, Ulugan.

630
01:07:47,566 --> 01:07:49,645
I will never give this chair to him.

631
01:08:00,326 --> 01:08:02,005
Come, Osman.

632
01:08:03,846 --> 01:08:05,245
Come.

633
01:08:12,646 --> 01:08:14,565
I still can't believe what happened.

634
01:08:17,805 --> 01:08:19,725
My Allah.

635
01:08:26,966 --> 01:08:28,484
I had no one.

636
01:08:30,725 --> 01:08:32,285
She became my mother.

637
01:08:35,566 --> 01:08:37,725
She never broke my heart.

638
01:08:39,486 --> 01:08:42,845
No one was ever kind to me like her.

639
01:08:43,086 --> 01:08:45,125
May God give us strength.

640
01:09:00,166 --> 01:09:01,685
How is my father?

641
01:09:03,206 --> 01:09:04,285
My father?

642
01:09:08,006 --> 01:09:09,564
Good.

643
01:09:10,606 --> 01:09:13,604
We left him with my mother.

644
01:09:39,326 --> 01:09:43,365
Brother, did my mother suffer a lot?

645
01:09:50,526 --> 01:09:52,165
Fatma...

646
01:09:54,326 --> 01:09:56,285
My mother became a martyr.

647
01:09:57,606 --> 01:09:59,325
She became The Messenger of Allah's...

648
01:10:01,326 --> 01:10:03,565
...neighbour, God willing.

649
01:10:04,566 --> 01:10:06,205
God willing..

650
01:10:07,286 --> 01:10:10,125
God willing, tomorrow,
when we take the tribe back...

651
01:10:12,846 --> 01:10:15,525
...we will bury my mother next to my sister.

652
01:10:16,646 --> 01:10:21,045
At least she will reunite
with her Halime in her grave.

653
01:10:23,686 --> 01:10:26,805
My mother always kept Halime alive.

654
01:10:27,326 --> 01:10:32,725
She searched for my sister
for days, in the water and mud.

655
01:10:35,006 --> 01:10:39,245
Her heart burned from longing and pain.

656
01:10:42,126 --> 01:10:44,165
But my mother always stood strong.

657
01:10:46,646 --> 01:10:50,125
Your sister Halime...

658
01:10:51,526 --> 01:10:52,805
How did she die?

659
01:10:55,166 --> 01:10:57,925
We were children then...

660
01:10:57,966 --> 01:11:00,005
We were not there either.

661
01:11:02,366 --> 01:11:06,805
But I remember how my mother
was as if it were yesterday.

662
01:11:09,406 --> 01:11:11,805
Halime was playing by the stream.

663
01:11:13,446 --> 01:11:15,805
Then she suddenly disappeared.

664
01:11:17,846 --> 01:11:19,325
What happened after that?

665
01:11:20,046 --> 01:11:21,525
For days...

666
01:11:22,126 --> 01:11:26,805
...she searched for my sister in
the water, without eating or drinking.

667
01:11:30,126 --> 01:11:32,445
Then, she found my sister's lifeless body.

668
01:11:37,166 --> 01:11:40,485
My mother never looked the same again.

669
01:11:42,086 --> 01:11:43,685
She never smiled.

670
01:11:47,566 --> 01:11:49,525
Come, my beautiful daughter.

671
01:11:50,086 --> 01:11:51,925
I will check on the sisters.

672
01:11:55,126 --> 01:11:57,885
My daughter, wait for me.
I will come back, alright?

673
01:12:00,326 --> 01:12:01,805
Halime.

674
01:12:02,526 --> 01:12:05,165
Your mother is waiting for you, Halime.

675
01:12:08,206 --> 01:12:11,925
Let go! Let go! Don't touch me!

676
01:12:14,486 --> 01:12:18,285
I said let go! -Bala...

677
01:12:20,686 --> 01:12:24,005
You look good for a dead woman.

678
01:12:24,886 --> 01:12:25,925
Good.

679
01:12:26,446 --> 01:12:30,045
But there is no one left to
take you out of here now.

680
01:12:31,006 --> 01:12:35,925
If I want, I can keep you here for years.

681
01:12:36,606 --> 01:12:40,125
What kind of evil games are you playing now?

682
01:12:40,966 --> 01:12:42,005
No...

683
01:12:43,486 --> 01:12:47,085
Even the devil cannot compete me, Bala.

684
01:12:47,166 --> 01:12:52,725
You never fought bravely,
Sofia. You are just a coward.

685
01:12:52,726 --> 01:12:55,085
No one can make me upset right now, Bala.

686
01:12:56,126 --> 01:12:59,325
I have waited years for this moment.

687
01:12:59,806 --> 01:13:04,245
First you, then Osman. I
will kill you both together.

688
01:13:04,526 --> 01:13:08,725
Never. You will never be able to do that, Sofia.

689
01:13:08,726 --> 01:13:11,165
We have seen many cowards like you.

690
01:13:11,166 --> 01:13:14,603
We defeated all of them
with Allah's permission.

691
01:13:14,615 --> 01:13:15,765
Bala.

692
01:13:19,606 --> 01:13:23,085
I will hurt you so badly that...

693
01:13:23,086 --> 01:13:25,165
Hit me all you want, Sofia!

694
01:13:25,166 --> 01:13:27,925
Because you can only stop
me by chaining my hands!

695
01:13:27,926 --> 01:13:30,205
No, I will not hurt you like that.

696
01:13:31,206 --> 01:13:32,645
I will only...

697
01:13:34,326 --> 01:13:38,325
...tear off the scabs of an old wound.

698
01:13:38,326 --> 01:13:40,805
What are you saying?

699
01:13:43,566 --> 01:13:47,245
I told you about a secret, do you remember?

700
01:13:48,966 --> 01:13:49,765
Bala!

701
01:13:49,806 --> 01:13:52,485
Don't you want to know
the secret I will give you?

702
01:13:52,486 --> 01:13:56,685
Keep your poisonous words to yourself, you
demon! This time, you will not live long.

703
01:13:56,686 --> 01:13:58,605
I will take your life.

704
01:13:59,326 --> 01:14:02,165
What secret, what game
are you talking about Sofia?

705
01:14:02,166 --> 01:14:06,005
I will not fall for your secrets or your games.

706
01:14:07,206 --> 01:14:08,605
Are you sure?

707
01:14:09,206 --> 01:14:13,045
-So you are not curious about who it is about.
-I'm not!

708
01:14:17,286 --> 01:14:19,085
If Halime heard it...

709
01:14:24,526 --> 01:14:26,205
...she would be very sad.

710
01:14:32,086 --> 01:14:35,125
Her mother is not curious
about the secret about her.

711
01:14:35,126 --> 01:14:38,765
You snake! Don't say my daughter's name.

712
01:14:38,766 --> 01:14:40,885
Don't say my daughter's name, Sofia.

713
01:14:40,966 --> 01:14:42,965
My secret is...

714
01:14:44,326 --> 01:14:45,925
..little Halime.

715
01:14:46,766 --> 01:14:49,725
What are you saying, Sofia? Sofia, don't go!

716
01:14:50,646 --> 01:14:53,925
What are you saying, Sofia? Don't
go, come here! Sofia, come here!

717
01:14:53,926 --> 01:14:56,845
What are you saying? Don't
go, come here! Let me go!

718
01:15:20,086 --> 01:15:21,525
Bala..

719
01:15:39,366 --> 01:15:42,165
How many times have I come to this threshold?

720
01:15:46,126 --> 01:15:49,045
How many times have I
turned away from this door?

721
01:16:10,326 --> 01:16:12,245
Seeing you like this.

722
01:16:18,046 --> 01:16:20,805
Seeing you like this.

723
01:16:24,166 --> 01:16:26,165
Seeing you like this

724
01:16:28,286 --> 01:16:30,125
Do you think it is easy for me?

725
01:17:35,046 --> 01:17:38,205
Can Osman stand seeing you like this?

726
01:17:38,726 --> 01:17:40,965
Can he ever stand it?

727
01:17:43,206 --> 01:17:46,005
Your Osman would never leave you alone.

728
01:17:46,246 --> 01:17:48,525
He would never leave you alone.

729
01:17:49,046 --> 01:17:52,045
He would never leave you alone.

730
01:18:13,206 --> 01:18:14,405
Bala.

731
01:18:17,406 --> 01:18:19,925
If I can still stand here...

732
01:18:22,566 --> 01:18:23,685
...know that...

733
01:18:25,646 --> 01:18:27,645
...it is only for revenge.

734
01:18:38,166 --> 01:18:42,605
...take you to your daughter Halime.

735
01:19:05,606 --> 01:19:08,445
I will exist only for revenge.

736
01:19:11,526 --> 01:19:13,125
From now on...

737
01:19:16,766 --> 01:19:19,125
...only my sword will speak.

738
01:19:23,846 --> 01:19:25,605
Can I come in, my Bey?

739
01:19:28,486 --> 01:19:30,285
Come in, Cerkutay.

740
01:19:47,166 --> 01:19:49,765
-My Bey -Why?

741
01:19:50,166 --> 01:19:53,645
Why weren't you at the council...

742
01:19:53,806 --> 01:19:56,645
...when we were talking
about the attack, Cerkutay?

743
01:19:58,446 --> 01:19:59,525
Why?

744
01:20:00,926 --> 01:20:03,205
My Bey, after my carelessness...

745
01:20:05,126 --> 01:20:07,005
...how could I look at your face?

746
01:20:09,926 --> 01:20:11,605
My Bey, cut my head off.

747
01:20:12,726 --> 01:20:14,085
Take my life.

748
01:20:14,846 --> 01:20:16,125
With your own hands.

749
01:20:17,726 --> 01:20:20,245
I can no longer stand behind you.

750
01:20:23,206 --> 01:20:25,805
I can no longer breathe like this.

751
01:20:28,086 --> 01:20:29,965
I disobeyed your order first.

752
01:20:30,766 --> 01:20:32,085
Then..

753
01:20:35,486 --> 01:20:37,285
Then I couldn't..

754
01:20:38,406 --> 01:20:39,845
...protect Bala Hatun...

755
01:20:42,446 --> 01:20:44,085
...your trust...

756
01:20:44,526 --> 01:20:45,965
...from this fate.

757
01:20:48,886 --> 01:20:50,765
I know this pain, my Bey.

758
01:20:57,446 --> 01:21:00,365
Don't make me live with my head bowed.

759
01:21:00,446 --> 01:21:02,525
Get up.

760
01:21:04,406 --> 01:21:06,445
Get up Cerkutay.

761
01:21:13,486 --> 01:21:15,205
Don't kneel again.

762
01:21:16,206 --> 01:21:20,325
Don't you kneel ever again.

763
01:21:28,326 --> 01:21:31,205
I never had a doubt about
you, even for a moment.

764
01:21:31,566 --> 01:21:32,725
I know...

765
01:21:34,086 --> 01:21:36,845
...you protected Bala...

766
01:21:36,846 --> 01:21:40,005
...that you did your best.

767
01:21:42,646 --> 01:21:45,325
Don't... Don't...

768
01:21:45,886 --> 01:21:47,205
...ever...

769
01:21:49,006 --> 01:21:50,365
...kneel again.

770
01:21:53,286 --> 01:21:55,365
Now you will pull yourself together.

771
01:21:56,086 --> 01:21:58,085
You will become stronger.

772
01:21:58,086 --> 01:22:00,285
You will become stronger so that...

773
01:22:02,446 --> 01:22:05,405
...whoever did this cruelty to us...

774
01:22:06,566 --> 01:22:08,965
...we will make them pay for it.

775
01:22:36,966 --> 01:22:38,565
...my Bey orders.

776
01:22:43,486 --> 01:22:47,565
l am sorry for your loss, my Bey.

777
01:22:55,806 --> 01:22:59,645
-Mother, don't go.
-My Halime, my beautiful daughter.

778
01:22:59,646 --> 01:23:03,445
Your hands touched those herbs,
that's why this soup is delicious.

779
01:23:03,526 --> 01:23:09,645
In the depths of the forest,
a wolf was watching them.

780
01:23:09,686 --> 01:23:12,605
My Halime, my daughter.

781
01:23:12,606 --> 01:23:15,965
Shouldn't I be happy now?

782
01:23:15,966 --> 01:23:21,645
Alaeddin, Fatma, Orhan, Osman..

783
01:23:22,606 --> 01:23:25,125
They all suffer like I did.

784
01:23:26,886 --> 01:23:28,445
But I am also in pain.

785
01:23:31,846 --> 01:23:37,125
Why do I suffer when I see them?

786
01:23:38,646 --> 01:23:42,725
Great Jesus, help me.

787
01:23:43,646 --> 01:23:45,605
Ease my unrest.

788
01:23:49,566 --> 01:23:50,685
God..

789
01:23:52,126 --> 01:23:53,765
God, are you angry with me?

790
01:23:56,726 --> 01:23:59,365
Am I doing a mistake by asking for revenge?

791
01:23:59,806 --> 01:24:00,885
Why?

792
01:24:03,406 --> 01:24:06,445
I suffer when I see them like this. Why?

793
01:24:13,126 --> 01:24:15,285
...suffer even more seeing their pain.

794
01:24:17,486 --> 01:24:19,645
I feel lost

795
01:24:21,126 --> 01:24:23,245
Enlighten my path.

796
01:24:25,646 --> 01:24:26,885
Meryem.

797
01:24:39,246 --> 01:24:40,405
Are you alright?

798
01:24:41,406 --> 01:24:43,445
I was praying for Bala Hatun.

799
01:24:44,086 --> 01:24:47,205
You also loved my mother very
much in a short time, didn't you?

800
01:24:48,046 --> 01:24:49,405
Yes, I did.

801
01:24:51,446 --> 01:24:54,005
She treated me like my own mother.

802
01:24:55,166 --> 01:24:59,925
When I close my eyes, I see
her face instead of my mother's.

803
01:25:01,286 --> 01:25:03,045
That is how my mother is.

804
01:25:05,286 --> 01:25:07,525
She was a mother to everyone.

805
01:25:10,286 --> 01:25:11,445
Meryem.

806
01:25:13,886 --> 01:25:16,805
How did you endure the
pain of losing your mother?

807
01:25:18,606 --> 01:25:21,765
How will I endure my mother's pain?

808
01:25:22,326 --> 01:25:23,845
You will get used to it.

809
01:25:24,886 --> 01:25:26,325
You will get used to it.

810
01:25:26,886 --> 01:25:28,725
It will burn your heart.

811
01:25:29,206 --> 01:25:31,245
The pain will never disappear.

812
01:25:32,926 --> 01:25:35,325
It will never go away, Fatma Hatun.

813
01:25:36,166 --> 01:25:37,645
It never goes away.

814
01:25:42,886 --> 01:25:44,525
Alaca.

815
01:25:46,646 --> 01:25:48,325
Bala's gone.

816
01:25:48,966 --> 01:25:52,925
You're upset too, right? You are upset.

817
01:25:53,326 --> 01:25:56,445
I will look after you for her now.

818
01:25:57,726 --> 01:25:59,405
I won't leave you.

819
01:25:59,646 --> 01:26:02,645
What's going on? Alaca, calm down.

820
01:26:02,646 --> 01:26:04,965
Alaca, no! Stop!

821
01:26:05,166 --> 01:26:08,645
Alacaz where are you going? Alaca!

822
01:26:25,246 --> 01:26:26,805
Alaca!

823
01:26:31,246 --> 01:26:32,885
Alaca

824
01:26:33,766 --> 01:26:35,805
What's going on?

825
01:26:38,526 --> 01:26:40,445
Alaca!

826
01:26:50,126 --> 01:26:51,325
How?

827
01:26:56,446 --> 01:26:58,845
This is our tree.
Bala's and mine.

828
01:27:23,806 --> 01:27:25,685
Bala.

829
01:28:19,006 --> 01:28:21,245
Bala.

830
01:28:24,726 --> 01:28:27,725
You're alive. Is this a miracle?

831
01:28:28,086 --> 01:28:31,085
I'm alive, Osman. I'm not dead.

832
01:28:31,886 --> 01:28:33,885
You aren't dead?

833
01:28:37,406 --> 01:28:39,525
Thanks to Allah.

834
01:28:46,846 --> 01:28:48,725
Thanks to Allah.

835
01:28:57,206 --> 01:29:01,525
I was waiting for you.
Alaca has brought you to me.

836
01:29:02,446 --> 01:29:04,725
But I knew..

837
01:29:04,846 --> 01:29:10,645
Even if my Brunette Osman were in
his deathbed, he would come for his Bala.

838
01:29:10,726 --> 01:29:12,645
Of course he would.

839
01:29:13,366 --> 01:29:17,325
No matter where he is, he would come.

840
01:29:18,086 --> 01:29:20,165
I would, of course.

841
01:29:30,246 --> 01:29:32,485
I know.

842
01:29:34,206 --> 01:29:36,285
Brunette Osman...

843
01:29:37,526 --> 01:29:40,165
..will never leave his Bala.

844
01:29:41,166 --> 01:29:43,045
I won't.

845
01:29:59,086 --> 01:30:01,085
Bala.

846
01:30:09,646 --> 01:30:11,205
Bala.

847
01:30:13,806 --> 01:30:16,445
I wish I hadn't opened my eyes.

848
01:30:21,006 --> 01:30:23,085
I wish I had slept...

849
01:30:25,246 --> 01:30:27,485
...for longer.

850
01:30:28,086 --> 01:30:30,685
I wish I had seen you longer.

851
01:30:32,446 --> 01:30:34,365
Bala.

852
01:30:38,326 --> 01:30:40,205
Boran..

853
01:30:43,246 --> 01:30:46,005
-Yes, my Bey?
Any news about Alaca?

854
01:30:46,726 --> 01:30:50,245
Alps looked everywhere,
my Bey. But they couldn't find.

855
01:30:51,366 --> 01:30:53,045
She had a wound, my Bey.

856
01:30:53,366 --> 01:30:55,925
She must have died somewhere.

857
01:30:56,446 --> 01:30:58,125
Dead or alive.

858
01:30:58,846 --> 01:31:01,925
Bring Alaca to me.

859
01:31:02,286 --> 01:31:03,885
As you order, my Bey.

860
01:31:16,966 --> 01:31:22,125
My Allah, You are the
Most Merciful of the merciful.

861
01:31:22,606 --> 01:31:25,445
May You provide peace for my heart.

862
01:31:25,886 --> 01:31:28,485
And foresight for my mind.

863
01:31:29,006 --> 01:31:32,005
Is that snake playing a trick against me again?

864
01:31:33,286 --> 01:31:37,605
I take shelter only in You
and seek help only from You.

865
01:31:38,686 --> 01:31:41,485
Show me the truth, my Allah.

866
01:31:41,806 --> 01:31:44,765
Don't leave me to that demon.

867
01:31:45,726 --> 01:31:49,685
Aameen. Aameen.

868
01:32:04,086 --> 01:32:06,045
My Bey

869
01:32:12,326 --> 01:32:15,485
-What's the situation, my Bey?
-The intel turned out to be true.

870
01:32:15,726 --> 01:32:20,605
Ulugan made Byzantine heathens
join his nokers and is coming to Sogut.

871
01:32:20,606 --> 01:32:22,885
What is their formation? Did you observe?

872
01:32:22,886 --> 01:32:26,245
They' took a formation not to
be seen while approaching Sogut.

873
01:32:26,326 --> 01:32:30,405
Countless dogs are walking in one single line.

874
01:32:30,406 --> 01:32:32,565
They're coming through narrow passages.

875
01:32:32,646 --> 01:32:34,845
Just like I predicted.

876
01:32:35,366 --> 01:32:37,525
It's happening as I predicted.

877
01:32:38,246 --> 01:32:41,725
Shahzades will move in
one wing and we in the other.

878
01:32:42,886 --> 01:32:45,405
We'll hit them unexpectedly.

879
01:32:46,766 --> 01:32:49,085
Come on!

880
01:33:07,086 --> 01:33:09,205
We'll advance silently...

881
01:33:10,606 --> 01:33:14,565
...and stand against Osman like the death

882
01:33:15,286 --> 01:33:17,685
Ulugan, we are so many...

883
01:33:18,126 --> 01:33:20,685
...that the back side
are just leaving the tribe.

884
01:33:20,886 --> 01:33:23,045
Osman has no chance.

885
01:33:31,846 --> 01:33:35,205
Osman has left Sogut, Commander
Ulugan. He's coming here.

886
01:33:35,326 --> 01:33:39,165
-How many alps does Poor Osman have?
-Just a few.

887
01:33:39,326 --> 01:33:42,605
They can never challenge
your mighty army, Ulugan.

888
01:33:46,406 --> 01:33:50,765
A Bey spreads his reputation
around the world, but...

889
01:33:51,126 --> 01:33:53,805
...he makes a mistake due to a hatun

890
01:33:53,926 --> 01:33:56,325
...gets ambitious and loses.

891
01:34:05,006 --> 01:34:07,925
Nokers, today is the day of fight!

892
01:34:08,166 --> 01:34:13,565
To paint these lands with
blood and slaughter alps today

893
01:34:14,566 --> 01:34:17,205
...move forward

894
01:34:33,366 --> 01:34:34,845
Leave me!

895
01:34:36,886 --> 01:34:38,445
You dastard!

896
01:34:41,286 --> 01:34:42,965
Tie this dog's hands!

897
01:34:43,166 --> 01:34:45,725
Leave! Leave me!

898
01:34:45,926 --> 01:34:47,525
Leave me!

899
01:34:48,526 --> 01:34:51,965
This is the punishment of those
who lament for our enemies...

900
01:34:52,406 --> 01:34:55,285
...and who try to protect them!

901
01:34:56,046 --> 01:34:59,645
-Leave me.
-If Osman attempts to attack,

902
01:35:00,006 --> 01:35:02,365
...he'll hit the ones loyal to him.

903
01:35:02,766 --> 01:35:05,565
You traitors! You betrayed Kayi!

904
01:35:09,246 --> 01:35:11,805
You betrayed your own kin!

905
01:35:12,286 --> 01:35:14,605
You serve Mongolians!

906
01:35:14,846 --> 01:35:18,645
I'm not doing this to you! Osman is!

907
01:35:20,246 --> 01:35:24,405
If you see Osman as the head
instead of me, I will crush all your heads!

908
01:35:27,366 --> 01:35:29,805
You betrayed Kayi!

909
01:35:39,166 --> 01:35:41,085
You traitor dog!

910
01:35:43,166 --> 01:35:45,125
Dastard!

911
01:35:50,766 --> 01:35:54,725
Mine too, Ilbay Bey? Will you crush my head too?

912
01:35:58,686 --> 01:36:02,125
Ayse, didn't I tell you not to leave the tent?

913
01:36:03,086 --> 01:36:05,925
You think I will ignore your cruelty?

914
01:36:06,126 --> 01:36:07,285
Never!

915
01:36:07,286 --> 01:36:09,565
-I will resist with people!
-Go inside, Ayse.

916
01:36:09,686 --> 01:36:12,365
-Tie me here!
-Take her to the tent.

917
01:36:20,966 --> 01:36:23,605
Traitor! You betrayed Kayi!

918
01:36:25,166 --> 01:36:27,485
Dog of Mongolians!

919
01:36:30,966 --> 01:36:34,485
If you don't obey me, you can't exist!

920
01:36:34,966 --> 01:36:36,285
You should know that!

921
01:36:36,286 --> 01:36:39,885
-Shame on you.
-You betrayed Kayi.

922
01:36:50,646 --> 01:36:52,365
Halime.

923
01:36:53,206 --> 01:36:54,645
My daughter.

924
01:36:55,846 --> 01:36:57,645
Halime.

925
01:37:13,086 --> 01:37:15,405
You are curious, huh?

926
01:37:16,926 --> 01:37:19,125
I knew, Bala.

927
01:37:19,886 --> 01:37:22,245
I know you very well.

928
01:37:22,886 --> 01:37:25,285
What did you mean?

929
01:37:25,686 --> 01:37:30,885
What did you mean? What
secret? My deceased daughter...

930
01:37:33,926 --> 01:37:35,685
Sofia.

931
01:37:37,086 --> 01:37:41,765
I came back long time ago. You know that, Bala?

932
01:37:44,726 --> 01:37:46,805
I saw your daughter.

933
01:37:53,926 --> 01:37:56,405
Was it you who killed her?

934
01:37:56,886 --> 01:37:58,405
Did you kill her, Sofia?

935
01:37:58,526 --> 01:38:01,685
If so, I will kill you terribly!

936
01:38:02,606 --> 01:38:04,685
Am I such a person?

937
01:38:04,966 --> 01:38:07,685
I came back to help you meet your daughter.

938
01:38:07,966 --> 01:38:09,605
What do you mean?

939
01:38:09,646 --> 01:38:12,205
Are you playing with my mind, Sofia?

940
01:38:13,446 --> 01:38:15,605
Your daughter is alive, Bala.

941
01:38:16,206 --> 01:38:17,765
Halime is alive.

942
01:38:17,926 --> 01:38:21,605
My daughter is dead,
Sofia! You're lying! Go away!

943
01:38:21,806 --> 01:38:24,525
Get out of here!
You're lying!

944
01:38:24,846 --> 01:38:27,285
Go! Go!

945
01:38:30,446 --> 01:38:32,245
Your daughter.

946
01:38:33,366 --> 01:38:34,685
Your daughter...

947
01:38:36,406 --> 01:38:38,965
...loves eating apples, right?

948
01:38:42,846 --> 01:38:47,205
And she's very fond of her damn father.

949
01:38:54,966 --> 01:38:56,805
Look, Bala.

950
01:39:06,326 --> 01:39:07,845
Do you remember?

951
01:39:07,966 --> 01:39:11,485
How did you get that?

952
01:39:11,486 --> 01:39:14,725
How did you get that talisman, Sofia?

953
01:39:14,846 --> 01:39:19,445
-How did you get that?
-It's Halime's talisman, right?

954
01:39:23,206 --> 01:39:26,405
No, Sofia. Give it to me.

955
01:39:26,686 --> 01:39:30,485
How did you get that,
Sofia? How did you get that?

956
01:39:30,846 --> 01:39:33,005
I've been..

957
01:39:34,086 --> 01:39:37,325
I've been waiting for this moment, Bala.

958
01:39:37,726 --> 01:39:40,525
Sofia! Give it to me!

959
01:39:40,806 --> 01:39:45,965
How did you get that? No! No!

960
01:40:03,326 --> 01:40:05,485
Like my father said.

961
01:40:06,246 --> 01:40:08,805
...they are moving like a snake.

962
01:40:08,966 --> 01:40:11,485
Byzantine soldiers and Mongolians...

963
01:40:11,926 --> 01:40:12,805
While walking through this route,

964
01:40:12,806 --> 01:40:14,965
While walking through this route.

965
01:40:15,206 --> 01:40:18,485
...they will follow this thin path.

966
01:40:19,126 --> 01:40:22,245
They'll move like a snake here.

967
01:40:23,206 --> 01:40:27,045
But the snake will be so long

968
01:40:27,966 --> 01:40:30,645
...that the head won't realize...

969
01:40:31,206 --> 01:40:33,565
...when we cut off the tail.

970
01:40:35,086 --> 01:40:38,805
While Ulugan goes in the front.

971
01:40:39,206 --> 01:40:41,805
...we'll start attacking.

972
01:40:42,806 --> 01:40:44,805
We will divide them first.

973
01:40:45,086 --> 01:40:48,405
We'll tear them apart slowly.

974
01:40:49,806 --> 01:40:52,685
Alaaddin, you got my back.

975
01:40:52,926 --> 01:40:56,445
Saruca, you get the end of the tail.

976
01:40:56,646 --> 01:41:00,005
Here we go. May Allah bless our fight.

977
01:41:03,646 --> 01:41:05,685
Let's go.

978
01:41:19,766 --> 01:41:22,165
For vengeance, attack!

979
01:41:22,246 --> 01:41:25,045
-Allah is the greatest!
-Allah is the greatest!

980
01:41:34,406 --> 01:41:35,725
Come on, alps!

981
01:41:35,766 --> 01:41:39,525
-Show no mercy! Allah is the greatest!
-Ya Allah!

982
01:41:42,726 --> 01:41:44,685
In the name of Allah!

983
01:41:53,966 --> 01:41:55,965
Allah is the greatest!

984
01:42:20,446 --> 01:42:23,845
Allah is the greatest! Come on

985
01:42:24,926 --> 01:42:28,485
Come on! We'll join Alaaddin Bey.

986
01:42:39,126 --> 01:42:41,925
-Come on, Alps!
-Allah is the greatest!

987
01:42:41,966 --> 01:42:45,245
Allah is the greatest!

988
01:43:01,046 --> 01:43:04,805
I swear I'll kill all of you. All of you!

989
01:43:08,486 --> 01:43:11,325
Ulugan's army must have
scattered by now, my Bey.

990
01:43:11,726 --> 01:43:14,125
Ulugan won't live for long.

991
01:43:14,246 --> 01:43:16,045
He will wait for his death now.

992
01:43:16,046 --> 01:43:19,005
Ulugan dog thinks we will face him.

993
01:43:19,006 --> 01:43:22,143
But with Allah's permission,
we will take our tribe back.

994
01:43:22,155 --> 01:43:23,205
We will.

995
01:43:23,526 --> 01:43:25,045
Sure we will.

996
01:43:34,766 --> 01:43:38,925
They are using the innocent people
as shields at the gates, my Bey.

997
01:43:39,726 --> 01:43:40,805
Right.

998
01:43:41,366 --> 01:43:42,485
Right.

999
01:43:42,606 --> 01:43:45,405
Now they think we will come through the gate.

1000
01:43:45,406 --> 01:43:47,205
But Turks are wolves.

1001
01:43:47,206 --> 01:43:49,005
They are as sharp as swords.

1002
01:43:49,006 --> 01:43:51,765
We will attack them from
where they least expect.

1003
01:43:51,966 --> 01:43:53,085
Archers!

1004
01:44:09,166 --> 01:44:11,845
Once the sword is drawn from its sheath...

1005
01:44:12,766 --> 01:44:15,565
...it is never put back in it without bloodshed.

1006
01:44:16,006 --> 01:44:19,245
Wolves have now risen.

1007
01:44:19,686 --> 01:44:20,885
Now..

1008
01:44:20,886 --> 01:44:24,125
Now, these infidels will only see blood...

1009
01:44:24,286 --> 01:44:27,965
...they won't see another day. Don't...

1010
01:44:28,126 --> 01:44:30,765
Don't hurt the people.

1011
01:44:31,006 --> 01:44:32,645
With Allah's permission, my Bey.

1012
01:44:38,446 --> 01:44:39,805
Archers!

1013
01:44:44,966 --> 01:44:46,085
Shoot!

1014
01:45:04,886 --> 01:45:08,685
Come on valiants! Kill
all the infidels! Ya Allah!

1015
01:45:10,966 --> 01:45:13,685
Attack!

1016
01:45:23,046 --> 01:45:24,885
What do you mean Sofia?

1017
01:45:24,886 --> 01:45:26,205
Is Halime alive, huh?

1018
01:45:26,206 --> 01:45:29,725
Why do you... Why do you have
that jawshan? Tell me something

1019
01:45:29,726 --> 01:45:31,645
Sofia, talk to me! Is Halime alive?

1020
01:45:31,646 --> 01:45:34,685
Tell me! Is she alive?

1021
01:45:34,686 --> 01:45:36,525
Talk to me Sofia!

1022
01:45:38,726 --> 01:45:39,965
She is alive.

1023
01:45:51,246 --> 01:45:53,085
I kidnapped her Bala.

1024
01:45:55,846 --> 01:45:58,005
I raised her like my own daughter...

1025
01:45:59,046 --> 01:46:01,565
...like a Christian.

1026
01:46:04,086 --> 01:46:05,285
You..

1027
01:46:09,046 --> 01:46:11,245
You...

1028
01:46:17,646 --> 01:46:20,805
...prevented the possibility
of me having children.

1029
01:46:30,806 --> 01:46:33,405
And I took your child!

1030
01:46:38,446 --> 01:46:41,805
And you...

1031
01:46:41,806 --> 01:46:45,085
...have cried for years at the
grave of a child you never knew.

1032
01:46:55,006 --> 01:46:58,805
Snake! Snake!

1033
01:47:00,686 --> 01:47:02,365
And I...

1034
01:47:07,046 --> 01:47:09,965
...killed you while you were alive, Bala.

1035
01:47:09,966 --> 01:47:12,125
While you were alive...

1036
01:47:14,006 --> 01:47:16,525
I will kill you!

1037
01:47:24,806 --> 01:47:28,325
I will tear out the heart of
anyone who touches my child.

1038
01:47:29,566 --> 01:47:33,365
How could you touch my gazelle-eyed daughter?

1039
01:47:33,366 --> 01:47:35,885
How could you touch her?

1040
01:47:35,886 --> 01:47:37,525
I will kill you, Sofia.

1041
01:47:37,526 --> 01:47:39,125
I will kill you.

1042
01:47:39,366 --> 01:47:41,245
Tell me, what did you do to her?

1043
01:47:41,246 --> 01:47:43,605
Tell me! What did you do to my daughter?

1044
01:47:44,366 --> 01:47:46,765
What did you do to her?!

1045
01:47:48,406 --> 01:47:50,165
Tell me!

1046
01:47:53,726 --> 01:47:56,365
Don't touch! Stay away!

1047
01:48:00,646 --> 01:48:01,805
Sofia

1048
01:48:09,406 --> 01:48:11,525
Let go! Sofia!

1049
01:48:11,526 --> 01:48:13,805
I will kill you with my bare hands, Sofia!

1050
01:48:13,806 --> 01:48:16,725
I will make you pay for the pain you caused!

1051
01:48:17,366 --> 01:48:19,445
I will make you pay for it, Sofia!

1052
01:48:19,686 --> 01:48:21,245
Let go!

1053
01:48:24,926 --> 01:48:27,645
Poena is here, ma'am. She is waiting for you.

1054
01:48:33,366 --> 01:48:35,445
Have a good rest, Bala.

1055
01:48:37,046 --> 01:48:38,565
When I return...

1056
01:48:38,726 --> 01:48:41,445
...we will continue our story, huh?

1057
01:48:42,046 --> 01:48:44,845
-You won't leave.
-Look at this carefully.

1058
01:48:46,046 --> 01:48:47,925
Am I telling the truth, huh?

1059
01:48:52,286 --> 01:48:54,525
Let her look at this carefully.

1060
01:48:55,966 --> 01:49:00,685
Sofia. Don't go! Give that to me!

1061
01:49:00,966 --> 01:49:02,085
Sofia.

1062
01:49:06,006 --> 01:49:10,085
You won't leave! Sofia come here! Sofia!

1063
01:49:18,366 --> 01:49:20,125
Halime..

1064
01:49:24,766 --> 01:49:28,965
Halime... No... no..

1065
01:49:39,406 --> 01:49:41,965
She is lying... She is lying...

1066
01:49:49,926 --> 01:49:51,365
My Halime...

1067
01:49:54,166 --> 01:49:56,405
It's really you, my daughter.

1068
01:50:00,046 --> 01:50:02,565
It's really you, my daughter.

1069
01:50:02,566 --> 01:50:04,685
My Allah... Keep me sane...

1070
01:50:10,166 --> 01:50:12,125
My Halime...

1071
01:50:14,686 --> 01:50:16,805
You are alive, my daughter.

1072
01:50:17,526 --> 01:50:22,325
You are alive, my dear...

1073
01:50:27,966 --> 01:50:31,605
Where are you? Where are you, my Halime?

1074
01:50:32,206 --> 01:50:34,805
I will find you.

1075
01:50:34,806 --> 01:50:37,965
I will take you. I will find you.

1076
01:50:43,526 --> 01:50:45,445
Our way leads to victory...

1077
01:50:45,486 --> 01:50:48,485
...and we are called victors! Alps!

1078
01:50:48,486 --> 01:50:52,965
Kill them with your dark
steel! Allah is the Greatest!

1079
01:50:52,966 --> 01:50:56,125
Allah is the Greatest!

1080
01:51:09,926 --> 01:51:11,365
It's a game.

1081
01:51:11,406 --> 01:51:13,205
Osman lured us into a trap.

1082
01:51:18,246 --> 01:51:20,725
I was waiting for you, dastards.

1083
01:51:20,726 --> 01:51:22,445
Come closer..

1084
01:51:22,926 --> 01:51:24,285
Come..

1085
01:51:27,006 --> 01:51:29,165
...get your share...

1086
01:51:29,966 --> 01:51:32,085
...from this dark sword.

1087
01:51:32,206 --> 01:51:35,205
Don't let any of them survive. Kill them all!

1088
01:51:35,206 --> 01:51:36,885
Come on! Move!

1089
01:51:40,246 --> 01:51:41,565
Come on Alps!

1090
01:52:03,046 --> 01:52:04,285
My Shahzade...

1091
01:52:04,806 --> 01:52:06,446
We need to go and help Orhan Bey.

1092
01:52:07,356 --> 01:52:10,405
-Now it is time to unite.
-Thank Allah.

1093
01:52:10,406 --> 01:52:11,805
You are right.

1094
01:52:11,806 --> 01:52:14,245
You are right
brothers. Come on then!

1095
01:52:14,246 --> 01:52:15,725
Come on!

1096
01:52:21,886 --> 01:52:23,765
What is that, dog Altuga?

1097
01:52:23,886 --> 01:52:27,045
You are scared like you see
the Azrael when you see me.

1098
01:52:27,046 --> 01:52:31,045
Orhan, your mother was burned alive but...

1099
01:52:31,046 --> 01:52:34,245
...you still don't know what pain is.

1100
01:52:34,246 --> 01:52:36,205
But I will teach you.

1101
01:52:50,806 --> 01:52:53,005
Osman is not around Commander Ulugan.

1102
01:52:54,326 --> 01:52:56,765
So you played a game, Osman.

1103
01:52:57,286 --> 01:53:01,525
You made us think you were
here, and now you'll attack the tribe.

1104
01:53:05,966 --> 01:53:07,965
The head of the snake is here.

1105
01:53:09,966 --> 01:53:11,045
Turhan.

1106
01:53:17,526 --> 01:53:19,165
Ya Allah.

1107
01:53:26,366 --> 01:53:31,085
Do not let these dogs survive! Come on! Nokers!

1108
01:53:35,606 --> 01:53:37,205
We are going to the tribe.

1109
01:53:37,766 --> 01:53:41,045
Demon... He realized it was a game.

1110
01:53:41,406 --> 01:53:44,485
We need to inform my father immediately.
-Alaeddin Bey...

1111
01:53:44,726 --> 01:53:46,125
I'll go.

1112
01:53:46,366 --> 01:53:48,325
Even if something happens to me...

1113
01:53:48,326 --> 01:53:52,965
-...I will be thankful.
-Thank you, Saruca. Go now.

1114
01:53:55,326 --> 01:53:56,485
Go after him!

1115
01:53:56,486 --> 01:53:58,125
Don't let him go to the tribe!

1116
01:53:58,126 --> 01:54:00,245
Get on your horses nokers! Come on!

1117
01:54:00,246 --> 01:54:03,125
Come on brothers! Attack!

1118
01:54:03,126 --> 01:54:05,645
Ya Allah!

1119
01:54:18,046 --> 01:54:21,725
I will slit your throat. Come at me, you dog.

1120
01:54:22,646 --> 01:54:25,805
You attacked my tribe!

1121
01:54:25,806 --> 01:54:27,965
You tortured my people!

1122
01:54:30,486 --> 01:54:33,485
I will drown you in your own blood!

1123
01:55:08,966 --> 01:55:10,725
Kill them, valiants!

1124
01:55:10,726 --> 01:55:14,370
Kill the dastard dogs and
send them away from our tribe!

1125
01:55:14,382 --> 01:55:17,205
Allah is the Greatest!
-For the revenge...

1126
01:55:17,206 --> 01:55:18,645
...of our Beys, our Alps...

1127
01:55:18,646 --> 01:55:22,085
...and for our martyrs! For freedom

1128
01:55:22,086 --> 01:55:24,005
For The Righteous!

1129
01:55:24,006 --> 01:55:27,405
Attack!

1130
01:55:50,246 --> 01:55:55,365
A Turk is worth a thousand jackals. Come, come!

1131
01:55:55,646 --> 01:55:57,205
Come, come!

1132
01:56:12,686 --> 01:56:15,805
I am coming, my Bey! I am coming!

1133
01:56:30,046 --> 01:56:31,165
Poena.

1134
01:56:33,206 --> 01:56:38,685
Why did you come here? -I don't know aunt.

1135
01:56:39,526 --> 01:56:41,005
I don't feel alright.

1136
01:56:42,046 --> 01:56:44,645
That family is making me feel this way.

1137
01:56:45,006 --> 01:56:47,525
What is wrong? Did something happen?

1138
01:56:48,446 --> 01:56:50,365
What is happening. Poena?

1139
01:56:51,646 --> 01:56:53,725
Did my mother ever cook Turkish food?

1140
01:56:56,046 --> 01:56:57,445
What does that mean?

1141
01:56:58,006 --> 01:57:00,205
I don't know, maybe she did.

1142
01:57:01,846 --> 01:57:03,925
Why are you asking me this?

1143
01:57:04,766 --> 01:57:07,165
I don't know. I don't know anything.

1144
01:57:07,646 --> 01:57:09,485
I am confused.

1145
01:57:09,686 --> 01:57:11,445
A smell, a moment...

1146
01:57:12,246 --> 01:57:15,525
It feels like I'm remembering
a moment I never lived.

1147
01:57:16,166 --> 01:57:19,125
It feels like I'm not the
person in those dreams.

1148
01:57:22,126 --> 01:57:23,205
Have you..

1149
01:57:23,926 --> 01:57:26,245
...not slept enough lately Poena?

1150
01:57:27,966 --> 01:57:30,245
Was my father playing games with me?

1151
01:57:33,086 --> 01:57:34,405
Sure..

1152
01:57:34,886 --> 01:57:36,405
...my little bird.

1153
01:57:37,566 --> 01:57:40,045
Your father, your mother..

1154
01:57:40,366 --> 01:57:42,365
...was taking good care of you...

1155
01:57:42,646 --> 01:57:45,045
...and doing everything for you.

1156
01:57:50,446 --> 01:57:52,445
You answer my question.

1157
01:57:53,806 --> 01:57:56,245
Did you drink the syrup I brought?

1158
01:57:57,286 --> 01:57:59,525
No, it broke before I could drink it.

1159
01:58:00,806 --> 01:58:02,925
Damn it. Poena.

1160
01:58:03,846 --> 01:58:06,645
I told you not to neglect it.

1161
01:58:09,086 --> 01:58:11,085
I'm sorry aunt, I...

1162
01:58:11,406 --> 01:58:13,205
...dropped it in that chaos.

1163
01:58:15,646 --> 01:58:17,645
It's not important my little bird...

1164
01:58:18,806 --> 01:58:20,925
...I am just worried about you.

1165
01:58:22,846 --> 01:58:23,765
Wait...

1166
01:58:35,566 --> 01:58:37,565
Here. Take it.

1167
01:58:38,166 --> 01:58:39,565
Take it regularly.

1168
01:58:40,526 --> 01:58:41,965
Keep it with you.

1169
01:58:45,686 --> 01:58:50,765
Once you get a good sleep,
everything will be alright.

1170
01:58:53,206 --> 01:58:54,805
What is Osman doing?

1171
01:58:55,686 --> 01:58:56,925
I don't know.

1172
01:58:57,486 --> 01:58:59,085
Everyone is devastated.

1173
01:58:59,086 --> 01:59:01,245
That's why I could easily come here.

1174
01:59:03,566 --> 01:59:05,565
They will get even more upset.

1175
01:59:10,526 --> 01:59:11,565
Come on.

1176
01:59:12,006 --> 01:59:13,485
Go now.

1177
01:59:27,846 --> 01:59:30,085
Is Bala alive, aunt?

1178
01:59:36,446 --> 01:59:38,605
You will kill her.

1179
01:59:38,806 --> 01:59:40,485
She is in the dungeon now.

1180
01:59:42,886 --> 01:59:45,565
-Can I see her?
-No, not now.

1181
01:59:46,406 --> 01:59:49,405
Come on. Go. Go.

1182
02:00:17,526 --> 02:00:19,805
I'll see Bala, aunt.

1183
02:00:23,806 --> 02:00:25,605
Come on!

1184
02:00:27,646 --> 02:00:29,845
Come to me, Ilbay.

1185
02:00:29,886 --> 02:00:33,485
If you don't care about yourself,
care about your people, Osman.

1186
02:00:33,486 --> 02:00:35,685
Drop your sword and surrender.

1187
02:00:35,726 --> 02:00:37,725
Turn around and look.

1188
02:00:39,566 --> 02:00:41,085
Come on!

1189
02:01:13,446 --> 02:01:15,005
Osman.

1190
02:01:15,846 --> 02:01:18,085
Your tribe will be your grave.

1191
02:01:18,446 --> 02:01:23,805
Your people and alps will
water your grave with their blood.

1192
02:01:25,806 --> 02:01:27,205
My nokers

1193
02:01:28,126 --> 02:01:31,165
We'll destroy Osman and his tribe.

1194
02:01:31,726 --> 02:01:36,165
We'll sow the seeds of eternal fear! Here we go!

1195
02:01:56,926 --> 02:02:03,645
My Halime drowned.
She drowned. How is this...

1196
02:02:04,566 --> 02:02:09,485
How? She drowned.

1197
02:02:31,566 --> 02:02:35,245
You have to tell me everything
Sofia. Tell me everything.

1198
02:02:35,606 --> 02:02:37,485
My Halime drowned.

1199
02:02:37,926 --> 02:02:42,125
I buried her with my hands. I don't believe you.

1200
02:02:44,566 --> 02:02:47,365
-Speak!
-Bala.

1201
02:02:48,526 --> 02:02:50,885
You are underestimating me.

1202
02:02:51,086 --> 02:02:53,965
Tell me everything, Sofia!

1203
02:02:58,166 --> 02:03:02,085
It was a time of war. You
were fighting in different parts.

1204
02:03:06,526 --> 02:03:10,005
I heard that you would go help the migrants.

1205
02:03:13,366 --> 02:03:15,645
It was the most suitable time.

1206
02:03:20,686 --> 02:03:24,085
You were going for help
when I attacked your caravan.

1207
02:03:24,566 --> 02:03:26,725
You couldn't have taken Halime with you.

1208
02:03:27,006 --> 02:03:30,845
-Ulgen Hatun, help me!
-My Allah!

1209
02:03:31,086 --> 02:03:35,685
While my servants were
stalling Ulgen, I took Halime.

1210
02:03:42,846 --> 02:03:46,245
You snake! You demon!

1211
02:03:52,166 --> 02:03:54,885
You know the rest.

1212
02:03:59,166 --> 02:04:01,365
For ten days,

1213
02:04:03,446 --> 02:04:05,765
...I watch you suffering, Bala.

1214
02:04:10,886 --> 02:04:12,805
Then...

1215
02:04:14,846 --> 02:04:18,925
I sent you a little girl looking like Halime.

1216
02:04:21,446 --> 02:04:23,845
She got swollen due to water.

1217
02:04:24,486 --> 02:04:26,805
You couldn't have recognized her.

1218
02:04:27,406 --> 02:04:30,005
Sofia, where is my daughter?

1219
02:04:30,366 --> 02:04:33,725
Where is my daughter? Tell me where she is!

1220
02:04:33,726 --> 02:04:36,525
I'll kill you, Sofia. I will kill you.

1221
02:04:37,726 --> 02:04:40,485
I will kill you!

1222
02:04:45,966 --> 02:04:48,285
Sofia, where is daughter?

1223
02:04:48,766 --> 02:04:50,845
Tell me where she is!

1224
02:04:50,966 --> 02:04:53,045
Tell me!

1225
02:04:55,726 --> 02:04:57,965
Finally, it's time to kill you, Osman.

1226
02:04:58,766 --> 02:05:02,165
Since the day I joined you, I've
always dreamed of this moment.

1227
02:05:02,446 --> 02:05:05,325
You aren't the first traitor who was one of us.

1228
02:05:05,566 --> 02:05:09,725
It's a pity that I will have my uncle
Sungur Tegin's blood on my hands.

1229
02:05:10,046 --> 02:05:11,765
You said you were a Kayi.

1230
02:05:12,206 --> 02:05:14,525
Your betrayed your own kin.

1231
02:05:14,926 --> 02:05:17,645
You aren't a Kayi at all.

1232
02:05:18,046 --> 02:05:19,765
You're the dark sheep of Kayi!

1233
02:05:22,046 --> 02:05:25,925
You say fancy words to cover your
weakness, but it doesn't affect me!

1234
02:05:26,206 --> 02:05:29,765
It will! I will take your life!

1235
02:05:30,046 --> 02:05:33,525
I will also cut
Begum into pieces!

1236
02:05:33,966 --> 02:05:36,325
Come to me.

1237
02:05:42,566 --> 02:05:45,405
Come on, come on, sisters!

1238
02:05:51,486 --> 02:05:54,085
-Move!
-Move, move!

1239
02:05:56,806 --> 02:06:00,405
What? What?

1240
02:06:10,246 --> 02:06:13,445
-My Bey!
-My Bey!

1241
02:06:16,046 --> 02:06:18,565
-What is it?
-My Bey!

1242
02:06:18,686 --> 02:06:22,525
What is it? Are my sons alright?
-My Bey...

1243
02:06:22,646 --> 02:06:25,565
Our plan got ruined. Ulugan is coming, my Bey.

1244
02:06:25,926 --> 02:06:28,405
-They are too many.
-What are you saying?

1245
02:06:34,006 --> 02:06:35,805
Saruca!

1246
02:06:41,246 --> 02:06:42,685
Osman!

1247
02:06:43,726 --> 02:06:48,365
Whoever protects you will
drown in their own blood, Osman.

1248
02:06:48,446 --> 02:06:50,805
You heathen dog!

1249
02:06:50,966 --> 02:06:52,845
You have a death wish, huh?

1250
02:06:53,006 --> 02:06:55,965
You thought you could fool me?

1251
02:06:56,206 --> 02:06:57,845
You were wrong!

1252
02:06:58,646 --> 02:07:01,605
Alps! Defending formation!

1253
02:07:01,926 --> 02:07:03,685
Alps!

1254
02:07:04,206 --> 02:07:06,765
Nokers, burn them!

1255
02:07:12,846 --> 02:07:15,045
-Split up -Come on!

1256
02:07:35,566 --> 02:07:37,245
My Bey.

1257
02:07:40,366 --> 02:07:43,605
-Osman Bey has fallen!
-Osman Bey has fallen!

1258
02:07:43,686 --> 02:07:45,885
Our Bey has fallen!

1259
02:07:45,886 --> 02:07:46,445
Our Bey has fallen

1260
02:07:46,726 --> 02:07:50,085
Osman Bey hasn't fallen but died!

1261
02:07:55,806 --> 02:07:57,685
My Bey.

1262
02:07:59,686 --> 02:08:02,405
My Bey, are you alright?

1263
02:08:02,526 --> 02:08:05,805
They are too many, my Bey.
Alps are dying one by one.

1264
02:08:06,366 --> 02:08:09,565
-Come on! Gather now. -We couldn't make it.

1265
02:08:09,726 --> 02:08:11,685
Gather, alps!

1266
02:08:12,166 --> 02:08:14,605
Follow me, come on!

1267
02:08:14,686 --> 02:08:16,325
Come on, brothers!

1268
02:08:16,366 --> 02:08:20,645
You can't run away from me in this world, Osman.

1269
02:08:24,686 --> 02:08:27,685
Nokers, go after them. Go!

1270
02:08:30,086 --> 02:08:32,125
Come on, come on.

1271
02:08:33,686 --> 02:08:37,205
-Cerkutay!
-Allah!

1272
02:08:51,646 --> 02:08:53,885
Let's go!
Let's go.

1273
02:09:00,886 --> 02:09:03,925
I will kill you, Sofia. Where is my daughter?

1274
02:09:08,686 --> 02:09:12,005
She always waited for
you, her brothers and father.

1275
02:09:13,366 --> 02:09:15,525
But you didn't come.

1276
02:09:17,806 --> 02:09:20,005
While Halime was crying

1277
02:09:23,086 --> 02:09:24,685
...you didn't come, Bala.

1278
02:09:32,166 --> 02:09:33,645
She was just little.

1279
02:09:33,726 --> 02:09:37,565
My precious angel was just little.

1280
02:09:37,806 --> 02:09:40,005
Just little, Sofia

1281
02:09:41,726 --> 02:09:43,125
Bala.

1282
02:09:44,006 --> 02:09:46,005
Yes, she was.

1283
02:09:46,286 --> 02:09:47,885
So it was easier.

1284
02:09:52,126 --> 02:09:56,645
I took everything from...

1285
02:09:57,406 --> 02:09:59,685
...your little angel.

1286
02:10:02,126 --> 02:10:06,885
Her name. Her memories and everything.

1287
02:10:14,806 --> 02:10:16,885
Halime..

1288
02:10:21,446 --> 02:10:23,645
My baby...

1289
02:10:25,926 --> 02:10:28,285
Halime doesn't know you, Bala.

1290
02:10:33,806 --> 02:10:35,445
Halime..

1291
02:10:37,366 --> 02:10:40,325
...is my girl now.

1292
02:10:49,086 --> 02:10:50,845
My baby...

1293
02:10:53,966 --> 02:10:55,965
She is my girl.

1294
02:11:11,886 --> 02:11:16,045
Hold on, brave man. We'll
check your wound. Alps!

1295
02:11:16,406 --> 02:11:17,845
Set the fire!

1296
02:11:18,046 --> 02:11:20,605
-My Bey.
-My brave man. Hold on.

1297
02:11:21,686 --> 02:11:25,165
Saruca... Saruca?

1298
02:11:28,206 --> 02:11:31,125
Time is up for me, my Bey.

1299
02:11:32,846 --> 02:11:35,605
I feel the fire in my chest.
-No.

1300
02:11:36,686 --> 02:11:39,285
No way! No way, brave man.

1301
02:11:39,406 --> 02:11:41,245
This wound can't kill you.

1302
02:11:41,566 --> 02:11:43,565
This pain...

1303
02:11:44,726 --> 02:11:46,445
It's different, my Bey.

1304
02:11:48,006 --> 02:11:49,605
I can feel it.

1305
02:11:50,246 --> 02:11:52,325
This is the death.

1306
02:11:54,046 --> 02:11:57,685
My Bey, my father Bayhan Bey used to say...

1307
02:11:58,886 --> 02:12:01,485
A brave man shows himself in the hard times.

1308
02:12:02,686 --> 02:12:05,445
Have I ever left you in a hard time, my Bey?

1309
02:12:08,646 --> 02:12:09,885
No.

1310
02:12:10,166 --> 02:12:13,485
You have never left me alone in hard times.

1311
02:12:13,686 --> 02:12:17,005
You've always gone first for me.

1312
02:12:18,046 --> 02:12:20,125
I'm pleased with you.

1313
02:12:25,766 --> 02:12:27,925
Thank Allah.

1314
02:12:30,686 --> 02:12:33,005
The fire in my chest is gone now, my Bey

1315
02:12:33,846 --> 02:12:36,085
I've heard these words from you.

1316
02:12:36,646 --> 02:12:38,445
So I can die gladly now.

1317
02:12:40,366 --> 02:12:41,885
My Bey.

1318
02:12:42,566 --> 02:12:44,925
I have a request from you.

1319
02:12:50,446 --> 02:12:52,125
Tell me.

1320
02:12:52,446 --> 02:12:57,125
I'm ready to do anything no matter what.

1321
02:12:57,686 --> 02:12:59,525
Tell me.

1322
02:13:11,806 --> 02:13:17,125
This is my father's hat. You gave me this.

1323
02:13:18,926 --> 02:13:20,765
My Bey.

1324
02:13:21,086 --> 02:13:23,485
Make them bury me beside my father.

1325
02:13:25,086 --> 02:13:27,645
Help me meet my father.

1326
02:13:29,166 --> 02:13:32,565
This warrior should be with his father.

1327
02:13:35,526 --> 02:13:40,085
I will find peace there.

1328
02:13:41,406 --> 02:13:43,405
God willing.

1329
02:13:52,126 --> 02:13:55,885
I bear witness that there is none
worthy of worship except Allah...

1330
02:13:58,486 --> 02:14:01,885
...and I bear witness that
Muhammad(PBUH) is His servant...

1331
02:14:05,206 --> 02:14:06,805
...and Messenger.

1332
02:14:15,766 --> 02:14:19,525
Indeed we belong to Allah,
and indeed to Him we will return.

1333
02:14:28,846 --> 02:14:32,445
Alps. You will fulfill his last wish.

1334
02:14:41,006 --> 02:14:42,045
My Bey.

1335
02:14:48,286 --> 02:14:49,325
Come on!

1336
02:15:00,646 --> 02:15:04,205
What are you doing here, Boran
Bey? Where is my father going?

1337
02:15:06,006 --> 02:15:08,045
We couldn't succeed, my Shahzade.

1338
02:15:08,846 --> 02:15:10,645
We did our best, but we failed.

1339
02:15:12,846 --> 02:15:15,085
We were about to take our tribe back.

1340
02:15:15,206 --> 02:15:17,205
Ulugan dog came.

1341
02:15:17,326 --> 02:15:19,165
They all came back.

1342
02:15:27,326 --> 02:15:29,765
Why are you standing there? What happened?

1343
02:15:31,006 --> 02:15:36,845
Wait, Shamil. Stop.
Brother... Brother... Saruca

1344
02:15:37,126 --> 02:15:38,325
Saruca.

1345
02:15:40,166 --> 02:15:41,605
Who did this?

1346
02:15:42,486 --> 02:15:45,605
Cerkutay Bey!
-We could not take our tribe.

1347
02:15:47,286 --> 02:15:48,525
Saruca...

1348
02:15:48,846 --> 02:15:50,405
...became a martyr.

1349
02:15:53,286 --> 02:15:55,285
And my Bey left.

1350
02:15:59,766 --> 02:16:01,365
I will take your revenge.

1351
02:16:02,406 --> 02:16:04,285
I will.

1352
02:16:05,206 --> 02:16:08,805
I swear, I will make them pay
for what they did to you, brother.

1353
02:16:52,406 --> 02:16:55,485
...the Ruler of the skies and the ground!

1354
02:16:55,924 --> 02:16:58,805
My Allah, I opened my hands

1355
02:17:00,646 --> 02:17:02,805
My Allah, please do not reject me...

1356
02:17:02,886 --> 02:17:05,445
Please do not reject me.

1357
02:17:05,806 --> 02:17:07,405
You ordered..

1358
02:17:13,526 --> 02:17:17,965
My Allah... I always trusted You.

1359
02:17:17,966 --> 02:17:20,205
I have always prayed to You!

1360
02:17:20,325 --> 02:17:25,843
May You... enlighten my way. May
You accept my prayers, my Allah...

1361
02:17:25,846 --> 02:17:28,683
May You accept my prayers...

1362
02:17:47,966 --> 02:17:49,045
Alaca.

1363
02:17:54,084 --> 02:17:55,165
Alaca.

1364
02:17:57,165 --> 02:17:58,405
Alaca.

1365
02:18:00,245 --> 02:18:02,125
Alaca. What happened?

1366
02:18:02,606 --> 02:18:05,084
Is it..

1367
02:18:07,966 --> 02:18:12,445
Is it good news? Is it, my girl?

1368
02:18:13,646 --> 02:18:15,045
Huh, Alaca?

1369
02:18:16,206 --> 02:18:17,525
What is happening to you?

1370
02:18:17,806 --> 02:18:20,645
Alaca, calm down! Alaca! Stop!

1371
02:18:20,646 --> 02:18:24,924
Stop! Alaca! Where are you going? Alaca!

1372
02:18:27,806 --> 02:18:29,125
Alaca..

1373
02:18:29,486 --> 02:18:31,843
You are sad because Bala is gone, right?

1374
02:18:32,245 --> 02:18:34,245
Your wings are broken.

1375
02:18:34,726 --> 02:18:36,683
And my arms are broken.

1376
02:18:37,046 --> 02:18:38,125
Right...

1377
02:18:41,406 --> 02:18:42,683
You are right.

1378
02:18:46,606 --> 02:18:48,645
Alaca!

1379
02:18:49,406 --> 02:18:54,565
Iltutan!

1380
02:18:54,766 --> 02:18:59,924
Where is Alaca going? Go after her! Alaca!

1381
02:19:12,286 --> 02:19:13,445
Alaca..

1382
02:19:18,966 --> 02:19:20,725
Alaca?

1383
02:19:55,966 --> 02:19:57,685
My dark Osman...

1384
02:19:59,326 --> 02:20:02,365
...never leaves his Bala alone.

1385
02:20:08,486 --> 02:20:10,045
Bala..

1386
02:20:19,246 --> 02:20:21,245
Alaca, is

1387
02:20:21,806 --> 02:20:23,205
Is it..

1388
02:20:25,726 --> 02:20:27,805
Is it good news?

1389
02:20:37,686 --> 02:20:38,965
Is she...

1390
02:20:47,886 --> 02:20:49,445
Is she...

1391
02:20:55,526 --> 02:20:57,285
Is Bala alive?